    thinking: "**Addressing Image Generation Failure**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag: the image generation quota is maxed out. My focus has shifted to the \"Zero-Broken-Image Policy\" outlined in the documentation. I\'m preparing to implement that policy, given the image generation failure, per the specific instructions.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Vector Graphics**\n\nI\'m excited about shifting to interactive SVG/CSS vectors! The fallback container approach allows for high-quality, interactive \"Proof Matrix\" UIs and live resume tailoring previews. Users can now click and test how \"Prove your fit\" will perform. I\'m focusing on building a design system with a warm cream canvas, forest green accents, and charcoal text.\n\n\n**Designing Landing Page Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of specific landing page elements. I\'m focusing on a clean, modern aesthetic with Plus Jakarta Sans typography, rounded cards, and subtle shadows. The design is intended to be responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile, adhering strictly to the top bar contract. I\'m prioritizing minimal animations and smooth transitions to ensure a streamlined user experience. The landing page itself will feature a sticky header, a hero section with a compelling tagline, and interactive elements explaining the value proposition.\n\n\n**Constructing Proof Sandbox**\n\nI\'m developing a \"Proof Sandbox\" visual engine, a split-view interactive tool. On the left, it displays a target job requirement; on the right, it shows how a generic resume transforms into an \"Architected Proof.\" Users can toggle between roles for live experience. I\'m focusing on \"The Architect Protocol\" methodology to deconstruct mandates, excavate proof, and blueprint executive resumes. It\'s live interactive, with a proof matrix feature.\n\n\n**Refining Landing Page Sections**\n\nI\'m now iterating on landing page sections, focusing on \"Match vs Prove\" comparisons and incorporating \"Proof of Impact\" elements with concrete metrics and detailed case studies. I\'m prioritizing clear pricing tiers with explicit feature breakdowns and prominent CTAs. I\'ve also just started designing the `/login` screen: it\'s intended to be a refined, high-trust authentication experience with a warm aesthetic and architectural split-layout.\n\n\n**Developing Login Flow**\n\nI\'m now deep in designing the login and signup flows, giving them significant attention. The `/login` page features a clean form with standard fields and convenient options, including single sign-on. The `/signup` page now has a structured registration with role selection. I\'m focusing on user-friendly password strength indication and seamless transitions to the preview workspace. Finally, I\'ve designed a clear preview view, which integrates FastAPI and Gemini AI tailoring endpoints!\n\n\n**Structuring Codebase Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a structured codebase. I\'m setting up `/src/types/index.ts`, `/src/services/api.ts`, and `/src/services/authService.ts`. I\'m creating context, common components, and landing page elements, including `/src/context/AuthContext.tsx`, `/src/components/common/Logo.tsx`, and more. I\'m focusing on defining FastAPI routes for response interceptors, base URLs and Gemini AI integration using strongly typed interfaces.\n\n\n"
