  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Landing Page Sections**\n\nI\'m now focused on building out the components for the landing page. I\'ve started by reviewing the required sections and their specifications. Specifically, I\'m working on the `Hero.tsx` component, ensuring the tagline and headline align with the provided guidelines. The headline sizing utilizes a `clamp` function for responsiveness. I\'m focusing on the first stage, the Hero stage.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the hero section components. I\'ve finalized the tagline: \"The Resume Platform That Turns Qualifications into Verifiable Proof.\" The subhead clarifies our value proposition, highlighting how we counter AI-generated resumes with verifiable evidence. Primary and secondary CTAs are in place, linking to the signup and interactive demo, respectively. I am also working on trust indicators. I\'ve designed a clean placement of trust signals below the hero.\n\n\n**Analyzing Proof Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into structuring the \"Resume Architect Proof\" to showcase verifiable claims. I\'ve designed interactive controls to dissect the proof\'s anatomy, focusing on scale metrics, engineering decisions, and business impact. I\'ve also outlined the \"3-Step Architect Protocol,\" and I am thinking about how to visualize it. I am also working on presenting a `ComparisonProof` for the next section.\n\n\n**Developing Social Proof Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating social proof to build credibility. I\'m building out `SocialProofMetrics.tsx` with metrics demonstrating improved interview rates and hiring manager credibility. I\'m focusing on the value proposition, and including concrete testimonials.\n\nI\'m now integrating social proof to build credibility. I\'m building out `SocialProofMetrics.tsx` with metrics demonstrating improved interview rates and hiring manager credibility. I\'m focusing on the value proposition, and including concrete testimonials. I\'ve designed a side-by-side analysis, contrasting keyword-matched resumes with proof-driven resumes to show the effect.\n\n\n"
