  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Core Request**\n\nI\'m now carefully dissecting the user\'s request, comparing its specifics against our existing implementation. I\'m focusing on the AI-powered resume analysis, which is the core of \"Resume Architect.\" I am pinpointing the precise instructions related to the product direction.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Core Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the *AI Resume Score Engine* as the central feature, ensuring it remains freely accessible. I\'m actively removing any pricing elements from the design, landing page, and navigation, aiming for a frictionless user experience. The design principles are also coming together: warm off-white, forest green, and charcoal tones for a clean, professional aesthetic. I\'m focusing on minimal animations and responsive layouts.\n\n\n**Refining Landing Page Design**\n\nI\'m now integrating neon colors and a futuristic AI styling into the landing page design. I\'m focusing on the \"Build, Improve, and Showcase a Resume That Gets You Hired\" message and its supporting taglines. Key components include the navigation bar with \"Get Started Free\" CTA. I\'m also highlighting the AI Resume Score Engine and other core features.\n\n\n**Defining User Onboarding Flow**\n\nI\'m now outlining the login and signup processes. I\'ve detailed the necessary fields for both the login and signup pages, including password visibility toggles and validation for a smooth onboarding. I\'ve also added a demo login for easy evaluation. The goal is to provide a clean and intuitive experience.\n\n\n**Establishing Authentication System**\n\nI\'m currently building the authentication foundation, implementing temporary local development for now. I\'m keeping the authentication logic distinct to prepare for FastAPI and SQLite integration later. Crucially, I\'m ensuring there\'s a clear notice to avoid misrepresenting local storage auth as a secure production solution.\n\n\n\n**Detailing Core Analysis Outputs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the specific outputs of the AI analysis. I\'m prioritizing the score breakdown into category bars, a list of missing keywords, and a comprehensive skill gap analysis (Found, Missing, Partial). Also, the system will need to generate actionable recommendations with impact badges. I must also emphasize that the system should never fabricate a score or randomly generate percentages. In a later development, the backend will calculate the score using a transparent method. I\'m focusing on providing a clean, non-randomized preview showcasing the scoring model using structured schema or an interactive template.\n\n\n"
