    thinking: "**Continue Development**\n\nI understand the core instruction now! I\'m focused on developing the Resume Architect project, and specifically, I won\'t be starting anything new or changing the existing landing page. The context is clear, so I\'m ready to move forward with the intended development.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Interface**\n\nI am now focused on defining the initial interface, specifically the authenticated Tools Dashboard and Resume History view. The design system is set: warm off-white, forest green, charcoal, clean white cards. I\'m prioritizing a clean, professional layout with a left sidebar and main content area and using the UI reference. I will avoid the \"avoid\" elements listed in the design requirements. The sidebar includes: Home, Create Resume and Review Resume buttons.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on the detailed design of the authenticated Tools Dashboard. I\'ve broken it down into a top bar with user greeting and quick actions, and the main content area. The main content will be split into a Quick Action Tools Hub with cards for the core tools and a Recent Resume Score and Analysis Spotlight. I\'m prioritizing clarity and easy access to the features. I\'ll make sure to use Lucide React icons for the sidebar items.\n\n\n**Detailing Resume History**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"My Resumes\" view, focusing on a comprehensive resume history. I\'m designing a table or card list with resume titles, target job details, modification dates, and compatibility scores. Action buttons will offer view/edit, re-score, duplicate, export, and delete options, with filters for easy access. Upload and create new resume actions are in progress. Profile and settings drawers are under consideration, too.\n\n\n"
