  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing intently on defining the project\'s scope, making sure I grasp the specific deliverables for this phase. I need to build the authenticated Tools Dashboard and Resume History interface exclusively. I\'m taking the Resume Architect UI as the source of truth, so I need to translate those finalized requirements into actionable tasks and components. I\'m now clear, I have to *only* build the specified features.\n\n\n**Refining the Design Parameters**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual design elements. I\'ve got my color palette defined: warm off-white, forest green, and charcoal. I\'m focusing on clean white cards and subtle borders and shadows to keep a professional look. I\'ve selected Plus Jakarta Sans for typography and tabular numerals for scores and dates. My main goal is to avoid gradients, neon, animation, pricing, and overcrowding. I\'m building a professional dashboard with a left sidebar, as I continue.\n\n\n**Mapping Sidebar Functionality**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the sidebar\'s structure and its connections to different views. I\'m noting the specific functions of each item, particularly how \"Home\" connects with the \"Tools Hub\" and other elements. I\'m focusing on user flow and mapping out quick actions like the resume creation and review processes from the sidebar, and I need to note how these are instantiated. I\'m thinking about the user experience with these links.\n\n\n**Clarifying Dashboard Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the functional components. I\'ve broken down \"Review Resume\" into launching the AI analysis modal with options to select from history and view the deterministic score. The \"Resume Editor\" has focused section management, and \"LinkedIn Optimizer\" features headline generation. I\'m building out a \"My Resumes\" history view for the user. I\'m detailing each item now, focusing on the functionality of the interface.\n\n\n**Detailing My Resume Hub**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"My Resumes\" history view, focusing on its display elements and actions. Each resume entry will show its name, style, a last modified timestamp, and a compatibility score badge. I\'m thinking I\'ll include quick actions like review, edit, duplicate, download, and delete. For empty states, I\'ll include a clear \"Upload or Create First Resume\" prompt.\n\n\n"
