  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Dashboard Layout**\n\nI\'m now focused on the dashboard\'s structure, starting with a left sidebar and a main content area, as requested. The sidebar will contain \"Home,\" \"Create Resume,\" \"Review Resume,\" and \"Resume Editor.\" I\'m ensuring everything is organized for easy access, and professional look and feel.\n\n\n**Defining Sidebar Navigation**\n\nI\'ve finalized the sidebar navigation structure. It will feature a collapsible design for mobile, expanding to 256px on desktop. I\'ve included a logo at the top and a navigation list with all nine items: Home, Create Resume, Review Resume, Resume Editor, LinkedIn Optimizer, My Resumes, Profile, Settings, and Logout, each paired with a Lucide React icon and a corresponding tab/view identifier. A user avatar card with candidate info will sit at the sidebar\'s bottom. Plus, a contextual breadcrumb will be in the top header.\n\n\n**Designing Main Content Area**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the main content area\'s visual design. I envision a warm off-white canvas, `#FAF8F5`, with a generous spacing and a max-width of 7xl. I\'ve also incorporated a quick actions button and a candidate status badge. I\'m prioritizing user experience within this section.\n\n\n**Refining Resume Preview**\n\nI\'m now integrating a preview of recent resumes, featuring quick actions. I\'m prioritizing the top three resumes with a direct link to the full \"My Resumes\" view. The focus is on quick access for the user.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nNow I\'m designing the \"My Resumes\" interface with a robust resume management system. I\'m including search, filter tabs (\"All Formats,\" \"ATS Minimalist,\" etc.), and sort options (\"Recently Updated,\" \"Highest Score\"). I\'ll have both table and card views for the resume list, displaying title, version, target role, format, score (color-coded), and last updated date. Each entry will have \"Review & Score,\" \"Edit,\" \"Duplicate,\" and \"Export\" actions.\n\n\n**Implementing Resume Functions**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features into the \"My Resumes\" area:  download of PDF and DOCX formats, including handling deletion with a confirmation modal. I\'m also ensuring a user-friendly empty state is present when no results are available.  The \"Create Resume\" modal will prompt the user to select a format, role, and company.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_539924"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React from \'react\';\\nimport { Logo } from \'../common/Logo\';\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../../context/AuthContext\';\\nimport {\\n  Home,\\n  FilePlus,\\n  Gauge,\\n  Edit3,\\n  Share2,\\n  FolderArchive,\\n  User,\\n  Settings,\\n  LogOut,\\n  X,\\n  ChevronRight,\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\n\\nexport type DashboardTab =\\n  | \'home\'\\n  | \'create\'\\n  | \'review\'\\n  | \'editor\'\\n  | \'linkedin\'\\n  | \'resumes\'\\n  | \'profile\'\\n  | \'settings\';\\n\\ninterface SidebarProps {\\n  currentTab: DashboardTab;\\n  onSelectTab: (tab: DashboardTab) => void;\\n  mobileOpen: boolean;\\n  onCloseMobile: () => void;\\n  resumeCount?: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport const Sidebar: React.FC<SidebarProps> = ({\\n  currentTab,\\n  onSelectTab,\\n  mobileOpen,\\n  onCloseMobile,\\n  resumeCount = 3,\\n}) => {\\n  const { user, logout } = useAuth();\\n\\n  const navItems = [\\n    { id: \'home\' as DashboardTab, label: \'Home\', icon: Home },\\n    { id: \'create\' as DashboardTab, label: \'Create Resume\', icon: FilePlus },\\n    { id: \'review\' as DashboardTab, label: \'Review Resume\', icon: Gauge },\\n    { id: \'editor\' as DashboardTab, label: \'Resume Editor\', icon: Edit3 },\\n    { id: \'linkedin\' as DashboardTab, label: \'LinkedIn Optimizer\', icon: Share2 },\\n    {\\n      id: \'resumes\' as DashboardTab,\\n      label: \'My Resumes\',\\n      icon: FolderArchive,\\n      badge: resumeCount.toString(),\\n    },\\n    { id: \'profile\' as DashboardTab, label: \'Profile\', icon: User },\\n    { id: \'settings\' as DashboardTab, label: \'Settings\', icon: Settings },\\n  ];\\n\\n  const handleNavClick = (tabId: DashboardTab) => {\\n    onSelectTab(tabId);\\n    onCloseMobile();\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleLogout = async () => {\\n    onCloseMobile();\\n    await logout();\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <>\\n      {/* Mobile Backdrop */}\\n      {mobileOpen && (\\n        <div\\n          className=\\\"fixed inset-0 z-40 bg-black/40 backdrop-blur-xs lg:hidden transition-opacity\\\"\\n          onClick={onCloseMobile}\\n        />\\n      )}\\n\\n      {/* Sidebar Container */}\\n      <aside\\n        className={`fixed top-0 bottom-0 left-0 z-50 w-64 bg-white border-r border-[#E5E1D7] flex flex-col justify-between transition-transform duration-200 ease-in-out lg:translate-x-0 ${\\n          mobileOpen ? \'translate-x-0\' : \'-translate-x-full\'\\n        }`}\\n      >\\n        {/* Top Header / Logo */}\\n        <div>\\n          <div className=\\\"h-16 px-6 border-b border-[#E5E1D7] flex items-center justify-between\\\">\\n            <Logo isLink={false} />\\n            <button\\n              onClick={onCloseMobile}\\n              className=\\\"lg:hidden p-1.5 text-[#57605A] hover:text-[#1C201D] hover:bg-[#FAF8F5] rounded-lg transition-colors cursor-pointer\\\"\\n              aria-label=\\\"Close sidebar\\\"\\n            >\\n              <X className=\\\"w-5 h-5\\\" />\\n            </button>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Navigation Links */}\\n          <nav className=\\\"p-3 space-y-1\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"px-3 py-2 text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[#848E88]\\\">\\n              Platform Tools\\n            </div>\\n            {navItems.slice(0, 6).map((item) => {\\n              const Icon = item.icon;\\n              const isActive = currentTab === item.id;\\n              return (\\n                <button\\n                  key={item.id}\\n                  onClick={() => handleNavClick(item.id)}\\n                  className={`w-full flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs font-semibold transition-all cursor-pointer whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 ${\\n                    isActive\\n                      ? \'bg-[#1B4332] text-white shadow-sm\'\\n                      : \'text-[#57605A] hover:text-[#1C201D] hover:bg-[#FAF8F5]\'\\n                  }`}\\n                >\\n                  <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2.5\\\">\\n                    <Icon className={`w-4 h-4 ${isActive ? \'text-white\' : \'text-[#848E88]\'}`} />\\n                    <span>{item.label}</span>\\n                  </div>\\n                  {item.badge && (\\n                    <span\\n                      className={`text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full ${\\n                        isActive\\n                          ? \'bg-white/20 text-white\'\\n                          : \'bg-[#F3EFE7] text-[#1C201D]\'\\n                      }`}\\n                    >\\n                      {item.badge}\\n                    </span>\\n                  )}\\n                </button>\\n              );\\n            })}\\n\\n            <div className=\\\"pt-4 px-3 py-2 text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[#848E88]\\\">\\n              Account & Setup\\n            </div>\\n            {navItems.slice(6).map((item) => {\\n              const Icon = item.icon;\\n              const isActive = currentTab === item.id;\\n              return (\\n                <button\\n                  key={item.id}\\n                  onClick={() => handleNavClick(item.id)}\\n                  className={`w-full flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs font-semibold transition-all cursor-pointer whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 ${\\n                    isActive\\n                      ? \'bg-[#1B4332] text-white shadow-sm\'\\n                      : \'text-[#57605A] hover:text-[#1C201D] hover:bg-[#FAF8F5]\'\\n                  }`}\\n                >\\n                  <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2.5\\\">\\n                    <Icon className={`w-4 h-4 ${isActive ? \'text-white\' : \'text-[#848E88]\'}`} />\\n                    <span>{item.label}</span>\\n                  </div>\\n                </button>\\n              );\\n            })}\\n          </nav>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        {/* Bottom Section: Candidate Status & Logout */}\\n        <div className=\\\"p-3 border-t border-[#E5E1D7] space-y-2\\\">\\n          {/* Candidate Card */}\\n          <div className=\\\"p-3 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5E1D7] flex items-center justify-between\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"min-w-0 pr-2\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-xs font-bold text-[#1C201D] block truncate\\\">\\n                {user?.name || \'Candidate\'}\\n              </span>\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] text-[#57605A] block truncate\\\">\\n                {user?.email || \'user@example.com\'}\\n              </span>\\n            </div>\\n            <div className=\\\"w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-[#1B4332] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold shrink-0\\\">\\n              {user?.name ? user.name.charAt(0).toUpperCase() : \'C\'}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Logout Action (Item 9) */}\\n          <button\\n            onClick={handleLogout}\\n            className=\\\"w-full flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-[#8C2E2E] hover:bg-red-50 rounded-xl transition-colors cursor-pointer whitespace-nowrap shrink-0\\\"\\n          >\\n            <LogOut className=\\\"w-4 h-4 text-[#8C2E2E]\\\" />\\n            <span>Logout</span>\\n          </button>\\n        </div>\\n      </aside>\\n    </>\\n  );\\n};\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create dashboard Sidebar component with all 9 required items and Lucide React icons\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create dashboard Sidebar component\"}"
