    model_api_content_id: "yeLkatXvEpOGqtsPtoHkoA0"
  }
  planner_response {
    response: "The **authenticated Tools Dashboard** and **Resume History interface (\"My Resumes\")** have been built for Resume Architect while strictly preserving the existing landing, login, and signup pages and adhering to the design system.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n#### 1. Dashboard Layout (`src/layouts/DashboardLayout.tsx` & `src/components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx`)\n* **Fixed Left Sidebar (256px)** on desktop with a sliding drawer for mobile devices.\n* **All 9 Navigation Items** with Lucide React icons:\n  1. **Home** (`Home`): Tools Hub, candidate overview stats, latest score analysis spotlight, and recent resumes.\n  2. **Create Resume** (`FilePlus`): Launches the resume creation modal.\n  3. **Review Resume** (`Gauge`): Launches the AI Score Engine compatibility review modal against any job posting.\n  4. **Resume Editor** (`Edit3`): Focuses on the resume bullet formulation workspace with evidence quantification rules.\n  5. **LinkedIn Optimizer** (`Share2`): Focuses on the LinkedIn narrative headline and executive About section optimizer.\n  6. **My Resumes** (`FolderArchive`): Displays the full Resume History repository with count badge.\n  7. **Profile** (`User`): Candidate profile details and target seniority levels.\n  8. **Settings** (`Settings`): Backend integration status (FastAPI `/api/v1`, SQLite, Gemini AI) and local storage controls.\n  9. **Logout** (`LogOut`): Clears authentication state and routes cleanly to `/login`.\n* **Top Header (`src/components/dashboard/DashboardHeader.tsx`)**:\n  * Contextual breadcrumb navigation (`Resume Architect / [Active Tool]`).\n  * Mobile menu toggle.\n  * Quick action buttons (`Review Resume`, `+ Create Resume`).\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Tools Dashboard (`src/components/dashboard/HomeOverview.tsx`)\n* **Welcome Banner**: Displays the candidate\'s name, active resumes count, and average match score across their portfolio.\n* **Tools Dashboard Hub**: Four interactive cards corresponding to the platform\'s core tools:\n  * **AI Resume Score & Reviewer**: Analyzes resumes against job specifications.\n  * **ATS Resume Builder**: Starts a single-column, ATS-conscious semantic draft.\n  * **Resume Editor**: Refines and quantifies work experience bullet points.\n  * **LinkedIn Optimizer**: Optimizes search-indexed headlines and narrative summaries.\n* **Score Engine Spotlight**: Live evaluation card showing the deterministic 6-pillar breakdown (82% Strong Match on Staff Systems Engineer).\n* **Recent Resumes Section**: Direct access to recent documents with quick actions to score, edit, or jump to the full history.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Resume History Interface (\"My Resumes\" - `src/components/dashboard/ResumeHistory.tsx`)\n* **Search & Filters**:\n  * Real-time search across title, target job role, target company, and skill tags.\n  * Format segmented control (`All Formats`, `ATS Minimalist`, `Executive Modern`).\n  * Sort dropdown (`Recently Updated`, `Highest Match Score`, `Title A\342\200\223Z`).\n  * **Card View & Table View Toggle** for flexible candidate browsing.\n* **Resume Cards & Table Rows**:\n  * Document Title and Version badge (e.g., `v3.2`, `v2.0`).\n  * Target Job Title and Target Company with building icon.\n  * Compatibility Score badge with color coding (Green for $\\ge 75\\%$, Amber for $65\\text{\342\200\223}74\\%$).\n  * Formatted last-modified date and word count.\n  * **Action Toolbar**:\n    * **Score Review** (`Gauge`): Launches the AI score engine modal for the specific resume.\n    * **Edit** (`Edit3`): Opens the resume editor.\n    * **Copy / Duplicate** (`Copy`): Clones the resume version with `(Copy)`.\n    * **Export** (`Download`): Modal with simulated PDF and Word DOCX downloads.\n    * **Delete** (`Trash2`): Confirmation modal with safe removal.\n* **Empty State**: Friendly prompt when no documents match the search or filter query.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Creation & Evaluation Modals\n* **Create Resume Modal (`src/components/dashboard/CreateResumeModal.tsx`)**: Lets candidates configure the document title, target role, target company, format (ATS Minimalist, Executive Modern, Technical Specialist), and competency tags. Automatically adds the new draft to their history.\n* **Review Resume Modal (`src/components/dashboard/ReviewResumeModal.tsx`)**: Select any resume from history, enter or paste target job requirements, and run the deterministic 6-pillar compatibility score (showing circular percentage indicator, missing keywords, and recommendations).\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Data & Services (`src/services/resumeService.ts`)\n* Implements CRUD operations for resumes (`getResumes`, `getResumeById`, `createResume`, `duplicateResume`, `deleteResume`, `updateResume`).\n* Pre-loaded with realistic benchmark resumes (Staff Systems Engineer, VP of Product, Cloud Architect).\n* Pre-wired for Python FastAPI `/api/v1/resumes` endpoint integration.\n\n---\n\n### File Structure Summary\n\n```\nsrc/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboard/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Sidebar.tsx             # 9-item sidebar with Lucide React icons\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardHeader.tsx     # Breadcrumbs & quick actions header\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 HomeOverview.tsx        # Tools Hub, stats, recent score & resumes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResumeHistory.tsx       # Full My Resumes repository with search/filters/actions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CreateResumeModal.tsx   # Modal for drafting new resumes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ReviewResumeModal.tsx   # Modal for scoring any resume against job specs\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 EditorView.tsx          # Resume Editor bullet quantification workspace\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LinkedInView.tsx        # LinkedIn Optimizer workspace\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfileView.tsx         # Candidate profile settings\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SettingsView.tsx        # Integration status & data controls\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 landing/                    # (Preserved exact landing page)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 common/                     # Logo, Button, Input, Navbar, Footer\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 score-engine/               # Reusable score engine components\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layouts/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardLayout.tsx         # Authenticated 256px sidebar layout\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 MainLayout.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthLayout.tsx\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardPage.tsx           # State manager for authenticated tools & history\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LandingPage.tsx             # (Preserved)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LoginPage.tsx               # (Preserved)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SignupPage.tsx              # (Preserved)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 resumeService.ts            # Resume history storage & CRUD\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 scoreEngineService.ts       # AI Score engine service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 authService.ts              # Decoupled auth service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts                      # FastAPI client\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts                    # ResumeItem, ScoreCategory, SkillGap, etc.\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to Run & Test the Application\n\n1. **Development Server**: The Vite dev server is running on `http://localhost:3000`.\n2. **Access Dashboard**:\n   * Navigate to `/login` and click **Quick Demo Login** (or visit `/app` directly).\n3. **Explore Sidebar**:\n   * Click **Home** to see the 4 Tools Hub cards, quick stats, latest score engine spotlight, and recent resumes.\n   * Click **My Resumes** to explore the Resume History interface:\n     * Test the **Search** bar (e.g., search for \"Go\" or \"Fintech\").\n     * Toggle between **Card View** and **Table View**.\n     * Filter by **All Formats**, **ATS Minimalist**, or **Executive**.\n     * Click **Score** on any resume to open the AI Score Engine modal.\n     * Click **Copy** to duplicate a resume, or **Export** to test simulated PDF/DOCX downloads.\n   * Click **Create Resume** to create a new resume draft.\n   * Click **Resume Editor** or **LinkedIn Optimizer** to inspect those dedicated tool views.\n   * Click **Logout** to sign out and return to `/login`."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Scope**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve confirmed that the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` tasks are both successful, showing everything is running smoothly. Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the initial user requirements to ensure strict adherence. It looks like the core work \342\200\223 the authenticated Tools Dashboard and Resume History interface \342\200\223 is the sole focus. I\'ve ensured no deviation from the existing design system or unnecessary additions like project creation or UI redesigns.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Architecture**\n\nMy focus is now on the precise dashboard layout. I\'ve mapped out a professional left sidebar with a fixed width for desktop and a mobile drawer. It will feature the nine specified items, each linked to a Lucide React icon. The main content area will include a breadcrumb header and quick action buttons. I\'ve also outlined the authenticated tools dashboard with greetings, metrics, a tools hub, and recent resume previews. The resume history interface is next.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **authenticated Tools Dashboard** and **Resume History interface (\"My Resumes\")** have been built for Resume Architect while strictly preserving the existing landing, login, and signup pages and adhering to the design system.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n#### 1. Dashboard Layout (`src/layouts/DashboardLayout.tsx` & `src/components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx`)\n* **Fixed Left Sidebar (256px)** on desktop with a sliding drawer for mobile devices.\n* **All 9 Navigation Items** with Lucide React icons:\n  1. **Home** (`Home`): Tools Hub, candidate overview stats, latest score analysis spotlight, and recent resumes.\n  2. **Create Resume** (`FilePlus`): Launches the resume creation modal.\n  3. **Review Resume** (`Gauge`): Launches the AI Score Engine compatibility review modal against any job posting.\n  4. **Resume Editor** (`Edit3`): Focuses on the resume bullet formulation workspace with evidence quantification rules.\n  5. **LinkedIn Optimizer** (`Share2`): Focuses on the LinkedIn narrative headline and executive About section optimizer.\n  6. **My Resumes** (`FolderArchive`): Displays the full Resume History repository with count badge.\n  7. **Profile** (`User`): Candidate profile details and target seniority levels.\n  8. **Settings** (`Settings`): Backend integration status (FastAPI `/api/v1`, SQLite, Gemini AI) and local storage controls.\n  9. **Logout** (`LogOut`): Clears authentication state and routes cleanly to `/login`.\n* **Top Header (`src/components/dashboard/DashboardHeader.tsx`)**:\n  * Contextual breadcrumb navigation (`Resume Architect / [Active Tool]`).\n  * Mobile menu toggle.\n  * Quick action buttons (`Review Resume`, `+ Create Resume`).\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Tools Dashboard (`src/components/dashboard/HomeOverview.tsx`)\n* **Welcome Banner**: Displays the candidate\'s name, active resumes count, and average match score across their portfolio.\n* **Tools Dashboard Hub**: Four interactive cards corresponding to the platform\'s core tools:\n  * **AI Resume Score & Reviewer**: Analyzes resumes against job specifications.\n  * **ATS Resume Builder**: Starts a single-column, ATS-conscious semantic draft.\n  * **Resume Editor**: Refines and quantifies work experience bullet points.\n  * **LinkedIn Optimizer**: Optimizes search-indexed headlines and narrative summaries.\n* **Score Engine Spotlight**: Live evaluation card showing the deterministic 6-pillar breakdown (82% Strong Match on Staff Systems Engineer).\n* **Recent Resumes Section**: Direct access to recent documents with quick actions to score, edit, or jump to the full history.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Resume History Interface (\"My Resumes\" - `src/components/dashboard/ResumeHistory.tsx`)\n* **Search & Filters**:\n  * Real-time search across title, target job role, target company, and skill tags.\n  * Format segmented control (`All Formats`, `ATS Minimalist`, `Executive Modern`).\n  * Sort dropdown (`Recently Updated`, `Highest Match Score`, `Title A\342\200\223Z`).\n  * **Card View & Table View Toggle** for flexible candidate browsing.\n* **Resume Cards & Table Rows**:\n  * Document Title and Version badge (e.g., `v3.2`, `v2.0`).\n  * Target Job Title and Target Company with building icon.\n  * Compatibility Score badge with color coding (Green for $\\ge 75\\%$, Amber for $65\\text{\342\200\223}74\\%$).\n  * Formatted last-modified date and word count.\n  * **Action Toolbar**:\n    * **Score Review** (`Gauge`): Launches the AI score engine modal for the specific resume.\n    * **Edit** (`Edit3`): Opens the resume editor.\n    * **Copy / Duplicate** (`Copy`): Clones the resume version with `(Copy)`.\n    * **Export** (`Download`): Modal with simulated PDF and Word DOCX downloads.\n    * **Delete** (`Trash2`): Confirmation modal with safe removal.\n* **Empty State**: Friendly prompt when no documents match the search or filter query.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Creation & Evaluation Modals\n* **Create Resume Modal (`src/components/dashboard/CreateResumeModal.tsx`)**: Lets candidates configure the document title, target role, target company, format (ATS Minimalist, Executive Modern, Technical Specialist), and competency tags. Automatically adds the new draft to their history.\n* **Review Resume Modal (`src/components/dashboard/ReviewResumeModal.tsx`)**: Select any resume from history, enter or paste target job requirements, and run the deterministic 6-pillar compatibility score (showing circular percentage indicator, missing keywords, and recommendations).\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Data & Services (`src/services/resumeService.ts`)\n* Implements CRUD operations for resumes (`getResumes`, `getResumeById`, `createResume`, `duplicateResume`, `deleteResume`, `updateResume`).\n* Pre-loaded with realistic benchmark resumes (Staff Systems Engineer, VP of Product, Cloud Architect).\n* Pre-wired for Python FastAPI `/api/v1/resumes` endpoint integration.\n\n---\n\n### File Structure Summary\n\n```\nsrc/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboard/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Sidebar.tsx             # 9-item sidebar with Lucide React icons\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardHeader.tsx     # Breadcrumbs & quick actions header\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 HomeOverview.tsx        # Tools Hub, stats, recent score & resumes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResumeHistory.tsx       # Full My Resumes repository with search/filters/actions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CreateResumeModal.tsx   # Modal for drafting new resumes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ReviewResumeModal.tsx   # Modal for scoring any resume against job specs\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 EditorView.tsx          # Resume Editor bullet quantification workspace\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LinkedInView.tsx        # LinkedIn Optimizer workspace\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfileView.tsx         # Candidate profile settings\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SettingsView.tsx        # Integration status & data controls\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 landing/                    # (Preserved exact landing page)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 common/                     # Logo, Button, Input, Navbar, Footer\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 score-engine/               # Reusable score engine components\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layouts/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardLayout.tsx         # Authenticated 256px sidebar layout\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 MainLayout.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthLayout.tsx\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardPage.tsx           # State manager for authenticated tools & history\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LandingPage.tsx             # (Preserved)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LoginPage.tsx               # (Preserved)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SignupPage.tsx              # (Preserved)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 resumeService.ts            # Resume history storage & CRUD\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 scoreEngineService.ts       # AI Score engine service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 authService.ts              # Decoupled auth service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts                      # FastAPI client\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts                    # ResumeItem, ScoreCategory, SkillGap, etc.\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to Run & Test the Application\n\n1. **Development Server**: The Vite dev server is running on `http://localhost:3000`.\n2. **Access Dashboard**:\n   * Navigate to `/login` and click **Quick Demo Login** (or visit `/app` directly).\n3. **Explore Sidebar**:\n   * Click **Home** to see the 4 Tools Hub cards, quick stats, latest score engine spotlight, and recent resumes.\n   * Click **My Resumes** to explore the Resume History interface:\n     * Test the **Search** bar (e.g., search for \"Go\" or \"Fintech\").\n     * Toggle between **Card View** and **Table View**.\n     * Filter by **All Formats**, **ATS Minimalist**, or **Executive**.\n     * Click **Score** on any resume to open the AI Score Engine modal.\n     * Click **Copy** to duplicate a resume, or **Export** to test simulated PDF/DOCX downloads.\n   * Click **Create Resume** to create a new resume draft.\n   * Click **Resume Editor** or **LinkedIn Optimizer** to inspect those dedicated tool views.\n   * Click **Logout** to sign out and return to `/login`."
