  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Request Depth**\n\nI\'m now carefully dissecting the components of this request. My primary focus is on grasping the implications of \"Allow users to add multiple experience entries,\" and how to translate this into a structured system. I\'m focusing on the specified fields: Organisation, Job Title, Start Date, End Date, Responsibilities, Ac. This parsing phase will inform my approach to the task\'s next stages.\n\n\n**Defining Core AI Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the system\'s core capabilities. The critical rule is becoming clearer; Gemini AI will refine *user-provided* information but not fabricate any content. This means focusing on its role in organizing, clarifying, rewriting, suggesting, and formatting. The \"Create from Scratch\" tab is the priority for now. The \"Improve Existing Resume\" tab is on the list for later.\n\n\n**Structuring User Inputs**\n\nI\'m now outlining the structure for user information input, including both personal details and experience. I\'m focusing on breaking this down into clear sections: Personal Info, Career Objective, Education, and Technical Skills. For each section, I\'m defining required fields, and the AI actions available within that section. For example, in Career Objectives, I\'m adding \"Generate Professional Summary\" as an AI action, but only using the user\'s information.\n\n\n**Outlining Experience Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing Sections E and F for project and experience entries, with multiple entries per section. I\'ve defined their respective fields and AI actions. Section E is Projects, with fields like Project Name, Description, Technologies, and Link, alongside the \"Improve Key Contributions\" AI action. Section F, Experience, will have fields such as Organisation, Job Title, Dates, and Impact, with the \"Rewrite Bullet Points\" AI action.\n\n\n"
