    thinking: "**Investigating Project Setup**\n\nI\'m now digging into the app\'s structure. I\'m checking for the presence of a `server.ts` file or evidence of Express integration. Next, I\'ll be reviewing the `package.json` scripts to understand how the server might be launched and managed. I\'m trying to determine whether this is a full-stack approach using server-side routing or if it relies on client-side calls to server endpoints.\n\n\n**Analyzing Vite Configuration**\n\nI see the `vite` command launches on port 3000. It looks like we\'re using Vite, and I\'m investigating how server-side Gemini integration might work within its architecture. We can either employ a Vite server middleware plugin, an Express backend, or a client-side Gemini service/server proxy using `@google/genai` with fallback mechanisms. The major capability constraint is already satisfied with `\"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]` in `metadata.json`, so I\'m pivoting. The `environment_constraints` suggests that we should leverage `.env.example` for environment variables and secrets.\n\n\n**Defining API Proxy Routes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the required API endpoints. Specifically, I need to create `/api/gemini/*` routes for the Gemini interactions. I\'m prioritizing endpoints for generating summaries, rewriting bullet points, and recommending skills. Since `server.ts` isn\'t present, the plan is to create it, implementing an Express server to handle these requests. In development, the intention is to use a `tsx server.ts` script. The goal is to set up a server-side proxy for secure API key handling.\n\n\n**Implementing API Improvements**\n\nI\'m now adding a `POST /api/gemini/improve-contributions` endpoint. My focus is on ensuring the client-side `geminiService.ts` handles the new API call, provides robust fallbacks for network issues or rate limits, and adheres to the strict requirement of never fabricating information. I\'m choosing `gemini-3.8-flash` for the text tasks, and I\'m setting up system instructions for the resume architect role, emphasizing factual accuracy and ATS clarity.\n\n\n**Confirming App Navigation**\n\nI\'ve confirmed how the \"AI Resume Studio\" fits into the app\'s navigation. The \"Create Resume\" sidebar item in `Sidebar.tsx` will now link to the AI Resume Studio page. I\'ve verified the page layout, including its title, subtitle, and tab structure for \"Create from Scratch\" and \"Improve Existing Resume\". I\'m also confirming the form sections for personal information and career objectives.\n\n\n**Structuring Resume Sections**\n\nI\'m now outlining resume sections for the \"AI Resume Studio\". I\'m planning out Education, Technical Skills, Projects, and Experience sections, each with specific fields and AI actions for enhancement. The goal is to provide a well-structured input form. I\'ll need to define fields for each section, including multiple entries for education, projects, and experience. Also, I am thinking through the API endpoints for actions like \"Generate Professional Summary\" and \"Improve Key Contributions\".\n\n\n**Designing Resume Preview**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the right-side live ATS resume document preview. I\'m aiming for a clear, single-column layout with standard sections: Contact, Professional Summary, Technical Skills, Work Experience, Projects, and Education. The goal is live updates as users enter details. I\'m planning \"Save to My Resumes\", \"Export PDF\", \"Export DOCX\", and \"Load Sample Candidate Data\" export controls. The live updating preview is a key feature and will export the resumes into the user\'s resume library.\n\n\n**Confirming Server Environment**\n\nI\'m now determining the optimal strategy for the backend. The framework guidelines emphasize using a `server.ts` entry point with Express when backend routes are required. This approach allows direct server-side integration of the `@google/genai` library if the `GEMINI_API_KEY` is present. I\'m verifying that if the key is missing or quota issues emerge, a fallback mechanism will be implemented for deterministic improvements.\n\n\n**Evaluating Server Approach**\n\nI\'m now determining the most effective approach for the server. I\'ve considered creating a `server.ts` file or opting for a lightweight server configuration. I\'m also examining how `vite.middlewares` can integrate with `server.ts`. I think this would require an Express server with an integration using the `@google/genai` library, with appropriate fallback strategies if the API key is unavailable or quota limits are reached. I am now exploring the integration to use.\n\n\n\n"
