  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'ve got a handle on the project\'s parameters. The focus is to build on the existing Resume Architect, not start anew. No redesigning either; I am sticking to the established foundation. Now, I will start to implement the unfinished user requests.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Core Features**\n\nI am now prioritizing the development of the crucial resume analysis system. My focus is on ensuring users can upload resumes, input job descriptions, and receive a comprehensive match score, broken down into key categories. Actionable recommendations are next on the list. I am focusing on seamless user input methods.\n\n\n**Implementing the Reviewer**\n\nI\'m making progress integrating the AI Resume Reviewer. I\'ve pinpointed its connection to the navigation, specifically the \'Review Resume\' item in `Sidebar.tsx`. I can provide dedicated endpoints for job description parsing, keyword matching, score calculation, and generating actionable recommendations. The plan is to use a weighted algorithm for scoring, with the specified categories and weights.\n\n\n**Designing the Reviewer View**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the interactive \"Resume Reviewer & Score Engine View\" within `DashboardPage.tsx`. My current focus is implementing the dual-column input setup. This will include options for resume input (PDF/DOCX upload, \"Pick from My Resumes\", paste text, and a \"Load Sample Resume\" feature), alongside a target job description input (paste text, job URL, \"Load Sample Job Spec\"). I\'m planning a prominent \"Analyze Resume Compatibility\" button to trigger the analysis with the six pillars.\n\n\n**Constructing the Score Display**\n\nI am now focusing on the \"Resume Reviewer & Score Engine View\" and building the master score banner. The plan includes a dynamic circular percentage indicator with an animation, a status badge showing match level, and the job title/company context. I\'m adding a quick compatibility summary, with options to download a report or re-evaluate with edits. I\'m also building a 6-pillar breakdown with weights. Clicking a category will expand the metrics. I will be incorporating a missing keyword inspector, categorized by importance.\n\n\n"
