  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Build the **Existing Resume Reviewer** and the central **AI Resume Score Engine** for Resume Architect (\"Don\'t just match the job. Prove your fit.\").\n   - **Deliverables**:\n     1. Resume input workflow (Upload PDF/DOCX, select from candidate\'s existing repository resumes, or paste raw resume text).\n     2. Job description input workflow (paste job spec text, input URL, or load sample job mandates).\n     3. Analysis trigger that calculates an overall match score out of 100 using a transparent, deterministic multi-factor formula.\n     4. Category-by-category score breakdown across the 6 evaluation pillars:\n        - Job Description Keyword Alignment (25% weight)\n        - Technical Skill Alignment (25% weight)\n        - Work Experience Relevance (20% weight)\n        - Project Relevance (15% weight)\n        - Resume Formatting & Readability (10% weight)\n        - Education Relevance (5% weight)\n     5. Identification of missing keywords with job frequency and criticality tags.\n     6. Skill gap analysis comparing job mandate context vs. detected candidate evidence.\n     7. Actionable, prioritized improvement recommendations with estimated score delta points and side-by-side Before/After bullet rewrites.\n     8. Option to export analysis reports or directly open/apply the findings in the AI Resume Studio.\n   - **Scope Boundaries**:\n     - Maintain established forest green (`#1B4332`), warm off-white (`#FAF8F5`), and charcoal typography (`#1C201D`).\n     - Do not create a new project or redesign landing, login, signup, or existing dashboard structure.\n     - Absolutely no pricing, subscription tiers, or billing engines.\n     - Never invent or hallucinate candidate qualifications; the scoring engine calculates scores deterministically through transparent weights.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in Previous Turns**:\n     - Global design system in `src/index.css` and typography in `index.html`.\n     - Landing page (`src/pages/LandingPage.tsx`) with Hero, 4 Core Features, Score Spotlight, How It Works, and CTA.\n     - Auth pages (`src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`, `src/pages/SignupPage.tsx`) with client validation and temporary dev auth (`src/services/authService.ts`).\n     - Reusable score engine display primitives in `src/components/score-engine/`: `CircularScoreIndicator.tsx`, `ScoreDisplay.tsx`, `CategoryScoreBreakdown.tsx`, `MissingKeywordList.tsx`, `SkillGapAnalysis.tsx`, `ImprovementRecommendations.tsx`.\n     - Deterministic 6-pillar formula and canonical benchmark data in `src/utils/scoreCalculation.ts`.\n     - Full-stack Express + Vite dev server in `server.ts` with `@google/genai` (model: `gemini-3.8-flash`) and `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` in `package.json`.\n     - Dashboard layout (`src/layouts/DashboardLayout.tsx`), Sidebar with all 9 items (`src/components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx`), Tools Dashboard Hub (`src/components/dashboard/HomeOverview.tsx`), and Resume History repository (`src/components/dashboard/ResumeHistory.tsx`, `src/services/resumeService.ts`).\n     - AI Resume Studio (`src/components/studio/` and `src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx` tab `\'create\'`) with 6 structured sections (A through F), live ATS document preview (`ResumeDocumentPreview.tsx`), and server-side Gemini AI assistance (`src/services/geminiService.ts`).\n     - All verification commands (`compile_applet` and `lint_applet`) have run with zero errors (exit code 0).\n   - **In Progress / Current State**:\n     - Planning and implementing the dedicated full-page **Existing Resume Reviewer & Score Engine View** (`src/components/reviewer/ResumeReviewerView.tsx`) to replace the modal-only trigger when selecting the `review` tab in `DashboardPage.tsx`.\n     - Adding the server-side analysis route in `server.ts` (`/api/score-engine/analyze`) and enhancing `src/services/scoreEngineService.ts`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - `server.ts` already runs with Express and Vite middleware on port 3000, importing `GoogleGenAI` from `@google/genai`.\n   - The user instruction explicitly specifies: \"The AI model must not independently invent the final score. The backend scoring engine will calculate it using a transparent, consistent scoring method.\" The formula is $\\text{Overall Score} = \\sum (\\text{Category Score} \\times \\text{Weight})$ where weights are 0.25, 0.25, 0.20, 0.15, 0.10, 0.05.\n   - `src/components/score-engine/` already contains high-grade visual components (`CircularScoreIndicator`, `ScoreDisplay`, `CategoryScoreBreakdown`, `MissingKeywordList`, `SkillGapAnalysis`, `ImprovementRecommendations`). The new Reviewer component should compose and orchestrate these alongside rich input tabs (Upload, Repository select, Paste text) and job mandate selectors.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - *Error*: `resource_exhausted` 429 when calling `generate_image`.\n     *Fix*: Adhered to Zero-Broken-Image Policy using custom architectural SVG geometry and styled CSS containers; no external image hosting used.\n   - *Error*: `tsc --noEmit` failed on deleted type `RoleComparisonPreset` in `InteractiveProofSandbox.tsx`.\n     *Fix*: Cleanly deleted outdated experimental files (`InteractiveProofSandbox.tsx`, `ArchitectureProtocol.tsx`, `ComparisonProof.tsx`, `SocialProofMetrics.tsx`) and verified clean linting.\n   - *Error*: `replace_file_content` chunk not found when closing `AuthLayout` in `LoginPage.tsx`.\n     *Fix*: Read exact line offsets with `view_file` and replaced the full file cleanly.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Runtime: Dev server running `tsx server.ts` on port 3000.\n   - Active Tab in Dashboard: Tab ID `\'review\'` in `src/components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx` maps to Review Resume. Currently it opens `ReviewResumeModal.tsx`. The goal is to build the full dedicated `ResumeReviewerView.tsx` rendered when `currentTab === \'review\'`, while keeping modal functionality for quick scoring from the History table.\n\n6. **Next Steps (Priority Order)**\n   1. **Create `src/components/reviewer/ResumeReviewerView.tsx`**:\n      - Step 1: Input Panel:\n        - Resume Source: Tabs for \"Select from My Resumes\", \"Upload File (PDF/DOCX simulated drag & drop)\", and \"Paste Resume Text\". Include a \"Load Sample Senior Resume\" button for 1-click testing.\n        - Job Description Source: \"Paste Job Spec\", \"Job URL\", and quick-load sample mandate chips (e.g. *Staff Distributed Systems Engineer @ Cloudflare*, *Lead Product Architect @ Datadog*, *Senior Full-Stack Lead @ Stripe*).\n        - Primary action: \"Analyze Resume Compatibility\".\n      - Step 2: Results Dashboard (once evaluated, with toggle back to inputs):\n        - Score banner with `CircularScoreIndicator`, grade, and job/file metadata.\n        - The 6-Pillar Category Breakdown (`CategoryScoreBreakdown`).\n        - Missing Keywords Inspector (`MissingKeywordList`) with category tags and copy affordances.\n        - Skill Gap Analysis (`SkillGapAnalysis`) comparing mandate context against resume text.\n        - Actionable Recommendations (`ImprovementRecommendations`) with Before/After rewrites.\n        - Action to \"Open & Optimize in AI Resume Studio\" (passes data directly to the studio) and \"Export Review Report (PDF)\".\n   2. **Add Server Route in `server.ts`**:\n      - Add `POST /api/score-engine/analyze` to use Gemini to extract matched keywords, missing keywords, and specific bullet recommendations, then compute the weighted category scores deterministically.\n   3. **Update `src/services/scoreEngineService.ts`**:\n      - Connect to `/api/score-engine/analyze` and ensure deterministic local fallback analysis when offline or when using sample inputs.\n   4. **Update `src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`**:\n      - When `currentTab === \'review\'`, render `<ResumeReviewerView />`.\n      - Wire \"Open in Studio\" action so reviewing seamlessly transitions to Studio editing.\n   5. **Verification**:\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to verify clean compilation with 0 errors.\n      - Test tab navigation between Home, AI Resume Studio, Review Resume, and My Resumes.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Design: Warm off-white (`#FAF8F5`), forest green accents (`#1B4332`), charcoal text (`#1C201D`).\n   - No pricing, subscription plans, or payment mentions.\n   - Do not alter or break existing landing, login, or signup pages.\n   - The AI must not invent the final score arbitrarily; compute scores deterministically using the transparent 6-pillar weights.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 307
