  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Resume Actions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how the application handles the \"Review Resume\" action. Specifically, I\'m examining the `handleSelectTab` function within `DashboardPage.tsx`. When the review tab is selected, it appears to activate the first available resume for review, though there\'s a safety check in place. I\'m noting the initial assumption that the first resume in the list is selected.\n\n\n**Refining UI for Review**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to enhancing the user interface for resume review. The initial modal approach feels inadequate. A dedicated view, specifically `<ResumeReviewerView />`, when `tab === \'review\'` is selected, offers a far superior user experience. This dedicated space allows for a more comprehensive and streamlined review process, crucial for the core functionality we\'re building.\n\n\n"
