  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt. My main focus is understanding the constraints: maintain the existing project, avoid new creations or redesigns, and keep established elements. The challenge is clear; to work *within* the provided boundaries.\n\n\n**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'ve scoped the core functionality, focusing on the resume analysis engine. The key features \342\200\223 upload, job description input, scoring, gap identification, and recommendations \342\200\223 are now clearly defined. My attention now shifts to UI/UX, prioritizing ease of use for the resume upload and job description input elements, and clear, actionable feedback.\n\n\n**Refining UI Workflow**\n\nI\'m now refining the \"Review Resume\" workflow. The current sidebar interaction directly opens a modal. My focus is expanding this; I propose a full-page `ResumeReviewerView` with distinct input modes: selecting from existing resumes, uploading files (PDF/DOCX), and pasting raw text. For job descriptions, I envision rich text input and job URL options.\n\n\n**Expanding Job Mandates**\n\nMy latest thought centers on rapidly loading job descriptions. I\'m building out a \"Quick-load Preset Job Mandates\" mode to streamline resume analysis. I envision options like pre-defined roles (e.g., \"Senior Full-Stack Engineer @ Stripe\") to allow for one-click analysis. The one-click API call, or local deterministic calculation, is the immediate next step.\n\n\n**Developing the UI Elements**\n\nMy current focus is on the detailed breakdown cards for each job mandate category, which will include score bars, matched keyword counts, and analytical summaries. I\'m also planning a panel to highlight missing keywords with importance levels, job frequency indicators, and copy actions. Additionally, I\'m working on a side-by-side skill gap analysis and actionable recommendations to guide improvement. I\'m also thinking through integration actions, such as direct connections to the AI Resume Studio and generating evaluation reports. Finally, I\'m checking if `server.ts` can use `/api/score-engine/analyze` with Gemini and JSON output with a calculation fallback.\n\n\n"
