  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Implementation Details**\n\nI\'ve taken a look at the provided types, which seem quite thorough and well-organized. Now, I\'m shifting focus to the implementation, specifically the API endpoint `/api/score-engine/analyze` in `server.ts`. My initial thought is to examine how to integrate the post route for that endpoint. Specifically:\n```ts\napp.post(\'/api/score-engine/analyze\', async (req, res)\n```\n\n\n**Defining Endpoint Behavior**\n\nI\'m now outlining the expected behavior of the `/api/score-engine/analyze` endpoint. I\'ve defined the required and optional input parameters: `resumeText`, `jobDescription`, `jobTitle`, `companyName`, and `resumeFileName`. The core of the analysis hinges on calling Gemini with structured prompts. It will analyze the resume against the job description across six key pillars, including Keyword Alignment, Technical Skills, and Formatting & Readability. The output will provide detailed insights like missing keywords and skill gaps, alongside actionable recommendations.\n\n\n"
