  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing API Endpoint Routing**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring correct routing between the client-side API calls and the server-side endpoints. Specifically, I need to verify that requests using `apiClient` or `fetch` are correctly routed to `/api/score-engine/analyze` or `/api/v1/score` depending on the setup, given the base URL configuration in `api.ts`. The primary concern is preventing conflicts or misdirected requests within the API structure.\n\n\n**Designing Workspace Features**\n\nI\'m now outlining features for the \"Existing Resume Reviewer & AI Resume Score Engine\" workspace. I\'ve designed a header section with titles, subtitles, and badges, and begun structuring Step 1: Input & Configuration Phase with tabs for resume source selection. I\'m focusing on user-friendly input options like saved resumes and file uploads.\n\n\n**Structuring Input Modules**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed designs for the input modules. Specifically, I\342\200\231ve completed the design of the resume and job description input tabs. The resume input supports multiple options, including text extraction, text pasting, and a quick sample resume loader. For job descriptions, there are also text paste and URL fetcher tabs, along with preset role mandates for rapid configuration and testing. I will now integrate this into the workflow.\n\n\n**Developing Score Engine Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing Step 2, the \"Interactive Analysis & Score Results Phase.\" I\342\200\231ve planned a \"Re-analyze or Adjust Inputs\" toggle for seamless input updates. A central \"Hero Score Summary Card\" is designed with a visual circular score and grade badge. I\'m also fleshing out the \"Score Engine 4 Deep-Dive Tabs,\" including the 6-Pillar category breakdown and the Missing Keywords Inspector. The keyword inspector will have filters for importance and frequency counts.\n\n\n**Detailing Skill Gap Analysis**\n\nI\'m currently designing the \"Interactive Analysis & Score Results Phase,\" specifically fleshing out the third tab, \"Skill Gap Analysis.\" It features a comparative table contrasting required job mandate context with detected resume evidence. I\'ve included tactical recommendations on how to substantiate skills without fabrication. The fourth tab, \"Actionable Recommendations & Bullet Rewrites,\" will be designed after.\n\n\n"
