  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Color and Typography**\n\nI\'ve got the core elements for the score engine nicely implemented, including all five components. I\'ve used Forest Green, warm off-white, charcoal text, and clean typography as requested. Now, I\'m thinking about next steps for a functioning resume reviewer.\n\n\n**Defining the Endpoint**\n\nI\'m focused on the `/api/score-engine/analyze` endpoint. I\'ll handle POST requests with resume data. If Gemini is ready, I\'ll leverage `gemini-3.8-flash` to evaluate those six crucial categories. Otherwise, a deterministic analysis with keyword extraction and benchmarks will be the fallback. I\'ve got both `/api/score-engine/analyze` and `/api/v1/score-engine/analyze` covered.\n\n\n**Constructing the Reviewer Interface**\n\nI\'m making progress on the `ResumeReviewerView` component, creating the full-page interface. The resume input section will have tabs for selecting from existing resumes, uploading files (PDF, DOCX, TXT with a sample resume button and a preview of extracted text), and pasting resume text with formatting and a sample resume button. The interface will include simulated parsing progress.\n\n\n**Designing Job Description Input**\n\nI\'m now implementing the job description input section. I\'ve got two modes: pasting the job description directly and entering a URL for fetching and parsing. I\'m also including one-click presets for common target mandates. The four presets are: \"Staff Distributed Systems Architect @ Cloudflare,\" \"Lead Full-Stack Product Engineer @ Stripe,\" \"Senior Cloud & DevOps Architect @ AWS Partner,\" and \"AI/ML Systems Platform Engineer @ Scale AI.\"\n\n\n"
