  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User\'s Request**: Build the **AI-powered LinkedIn Profile Optimizer** as an integral part of the existing Resume Architect application.\n- **Key Objectives**:\n  - Help students, freshers, and professionals improve their LinkedIn profile (headline, about, experience, projects, skills, certifications).\n  - Ground all generated suggestions strictly in genuine candidate information; **never fabricate** achievements, metrics, or qualifications.\n  - Page Title: `\"LinkedIn Profile Optimizer\"` | Subtitle: `\"Build a stronger professional identity and showcase your skills with confidence.\"`\n  - Two-panel layout: Left panel (profile input form & resume importer), Right panel (AI analysis, suggestions, TruthGuard review, and LinkedIn preview).\n  - Provide Manual Input (Personal Info, Headline, About, Experience, Education, Projects, Skills, Certifications) and Option B (Import from Resume Architect saved resumes).\n  - Deterministic/transparent LinkedIn profile quality score (separate from resume match score) across 7 dimensions (Headline, About, Experience, Projects, Technical Skills, Keyword Relevance, Profile Completeness).\n  - AI Headline Generator (up to 3 suggestions within LinkedIn character limits, copy/edit/accept/reject).\n  - About Section Optimizer (styles: Professional, Student/Fresher, Technical, Concise; side-by-side diff).\n  - Experience & Project Optimizer (action verbs, keywords, technical contributions, TruthGuard status: SUPPORTED, NEEDS CONFIRMATION, UNSUPPORTED).\n  - Skills & Keyword Analysis (EvidenceMap statuses: MATCHED, PARTIALLY MATCHED, NOT FOUND).\n  - LinkedIn Profile Preview (toggle between Original Profile and Optimised Profile, updating as suggestions are accepted).\n  - Save & Export (save drafts/versions, copy individual sections or complete profile, clear notice: *\"Resume Architect prepares optimised LinkedIn content. Review and manually apply the approved changes to your LinkedIn profile.\"*).\n- **Scope & Constraints**:\n  - Do NOT create a new project; do NOT redesign existing pages.\n  - Maintain the existing forest-green (`#1B4332`, `#2D6A4F`, `#EBF2EC`) and warm off-white (`#FAF8F5`, `#F3EFE7`, `#E5E1D7`, `#1C201D`) aesthetic.\n  - Build only the LinkedIn Profile Optimizer in this phase.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Earlier Turns**:\n  - Built full **AI Resume Score Engine** and **Resume Reviewer** workspace (`src/components/reviewer/ResumeReviewerView.tsx`, `src/services/scoreEngineService.ts`, `server.ts` API route `/api/score-engine/analyze`).\n  - Added interactive ATS diff viewer, heatmaps, ATS parser simulation, and printable executive audit reports.\n  - Passed `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit` passed with 0 errors) and `compile_applet` (build succeeded). Dev server running cleanly on port 3000.\n- **Skill Checked**:\n  - `gemini-api` (/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md) inspected. Use `gemini-3.8-flash` for server-side generation/analysis with structured fallback.\n- **In Progress for Current Task**:\n  - Reviewed requirements for LinkedIn Profile Optimizer.\n  - Ready to construct types, service/API endpoint, components, and wire into the top navigation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Architecture\n- **Navigation**: Top navigation in `src/components/common/Header.tsx` or `src/App.tsx` handles active tab/view switching (e.g. `dashboard`, `builder`, `resumes`, `templates`, `reviewer`). Adding `linkedin` as a first-class view tab allows seamless switching.\n- **Candidate Data Integration**:\n  - Resumes are stored and accessible via `ResumeItem` (`src/types/index.ts`) and `candidateProfileService` / `resumeService`.\n  - When importing a resume into the LinkedIn Optimizer, parse its name, target role, summary, work experience list, education list, projects, skills, and certifications into structured LinkedIn profile state.\n- **TruthGuard Integration**:\n  - TruthGuard checks evidence against source resume/profile. Each AI-generated headline, about section, or experience bullet receives a `truthGuardStatus` (`\'SUPPORTED\' | \'NEEDS CONFIRMATION\' | \'UNSUPPORTED\'`).\n  - Unsupported claims are flagged and never auto-applied.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- None encountered in this turn. Previous compilation and lint checks succeeded with zero errors.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Dev Server**: Running on port 3000 (`tsx server.ts`).\n- **Dependencies**: React 18/19, Tailwind CSS v4 (`@import \"tailwindcss\";`), Lucide-react icons.\n- **Environment**: AI Studio node environment with Express backend mounted with Vite middleware.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (Priority Order)\n1. **Define Types** (`src/types/linkedin.ts`):\n   - `LinkedInProfileData` (personal info, headline, about, experiences, education, projects, skills, certifications).\n   - `LinkedInAnalysisResult` (overall score 0-100, 7 category breakdown, strengths, weak areas, missing information, recommendations).\n   - `HeadlineSuggestion`, `AboutOptimization`, `ExperienceOptimization`, `ProjectOptimization`, `SkillEvidence`.\n   - `LinkedInSavedDraft`.\n2. **Backend / Service Layer** (`src/services/linkedInOptimizerService.ts` and `server.ts` route `/api/linkedin/analyze` & `/api/linkedin/optimize`):\n   - Deterministic transparent scoring + Gemini 3.8 Flash model prompt with comprehensive structured fallback.\n   - Genuine candidate grounding: explicitly instructs AI to only use candidate details and flag missing evidence.\n   - Headline generator (3 variants with char count \342\211\244 220).\n   - About section generator (4 style variants: Professional, Student/Fresher, Technical, Concise).\n   - Experience & Project optimizer with Before/After/Reason and TruthGuard validation.\n3. **Components**:\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInOptimizerView.tsx`: Main parent component orchestrating left/right panels.\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInFormPanel.tsx`: Tabbed or segmented input (Manual Input + Resume Import selector, personal info, headline, about, experience, education, projects, skills, certs).\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInAnalysisPanel.tsx`: Quality Score (7 categories with transparent weights), Strengths/Weaknesses, EvidenceMap.\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInHeadlineGenerator.tsx`: 3 headline suggestions, char counter, copy/edit/accept/reject.\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInAboutOptimizer.tsx`: Style selector, side-by-side comparison, accept/edit.\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInExperienceOptimizer.tsx`: Before vs After with TruthGuard badges.\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInProfilePreview.tsx`: Realistic LinkedIn card preview (banner, avatar, name, headline, location, action buttons, about, experience, education, projects, skills) with \"Original\" vs \"Optimised\" toggle.\n   - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInExportModal.tsx`: Section-by-section clipboard copy, full profile copy, draft version history, and manual-apply disclaimer notice.\n4. **App Integration**:\n   - Add `\'linkedin\'` view to `src/types/index.ts` (or `NavigationTab`), update `src/components/common/Header.tsx` to include \"LinkedIn Optimizer\" with a LinkedIn/Sparkles badge, and render `LinkedInOptimizerView` in `src/App.tsx`.\n   - Pass existing resume list (`resumes`) into `LinkedInOptimizerView` for instant 1-click resume import.\n5. **Verification**:\n   - Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`.\n   - Verify all features: manual input, resume import, quality scoring, headline suggestions, about rewrites across 4 styles, bullet rewrites with TruthGuard badges, preview switching, draft saving, and clipboard export.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Design System**: Forest green (`#1B4332`), warm off-white (`#FAF8F5`, `#E5E1D7`), charcoal text (`#1C201D`). Zero pill tags, elegant typography.\n- **TruthGuard / No Fabrication**: Never generate fictitious metrics or unstated job history.\n- **Explicit Notice**: Must include: *\"Resume Architect prepares optimised LinkedIn content. Review and manually apply the approved changes to your LinkedIn profile.\"*\n- **Keep Scores Separate**: LinkedIn Profile Quality Score is independent of Resume Match Score.\n</summary>"
