    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Continue developing the existing Resume Architect project.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n* Do not create a new project.\n* Do not redesign existing pages.\n* Maintain the existing forest-green and warm off-white design system.\n* Reuse existing components and navigation.\n* Build only the LinkedIn Profile Optimizer in this phase.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. OBJECTIVE\n   ==================================================\n\nBuild an AI-powered LinkedIn Profile Optimizer.\n\nThe purpose is to help students, freshers and professionals improve their LinkedIn profiles to present their skills, education, projects and experience more effectively.\n\nThe AI must use genuine candidate information.\n\nNever fabricate achievements, experience, skills or qualifications.\n\n==================================================\n2. PAGE DESIGN\n==============\n\nPage title:\n\n\"LinkedIn Profile Optimizer\"\n\nSubtitle:\n\n\"Build a stronger professional identity and showcase your skills with confidence.\"\n\nCreate a clean dashboard with two main sections:\n\nLEFT PANEL:\nLinkedIn profile information form.\n\nRIGHT PANEL:\nAI analysis and optimised profile preview.\n\nMaintain the same visual identity as Resume Architect.\n\n==================================================\n3. PROFILE INPUT\n================\n\nProvide two ways to enter profile information.\n\nOPTION A: MANUAL INPUT\n\nAllow users to enter:\n\nPERSONAL INFORMATION:\n\n* Full Name.\n* Current Job Title / Student Status.\n* Location.\n* LinkedIn Profile URL.\n* Target Industry.\n* Target Job Role.\n\nHEADLINE:\n\n* Existing LinkedIn headline.\n\nABOUT SECTION:\n\n* Existing About description.\n\nEXPERIENCE:\n\n* Organisation.\n* Job Title.\n* Duration.\n* Responsibilities.\n* Achievements.\n\nEDUCATION:\n\n* Institution.\n* Degree.\n* Specialisation.\n* Graduation Year.\n\nPROJECTS:\n\n* Project Name.\n* Description.\n* Technologies Used.\n* Project Link.\n\nSKILLS:\n\n* Technical Skills.\n* Professional Skills.\n* Tools and Technologies.\n\nCERTIFICATIONS:\n\n* Certification Name.\n* Issuing Organisation.\n* Date.\n\nOPTION B: IMPORT FROM RESUME\n\nAllow users to select an existing Resume Architect resume.\n\nAutomatically populate relevant fields from the selected resume.\n\nAllow users to edit imported information before generating LinkedIn suggestions.\n\nDo not claim to automatically access private LinkedIn profile data using only a profile URL.\n\n==================================================\n4. LINKEDIN PROFILE ANALYSIS\n============================\n\nUse Gemini AI to analyse the supplied profile information.\n\nEvaluate:\n\n1. Headline Quality.\n2. About Section Quality.\n3. Experience Description.\n4. Project Presentation.\n5. Technical Skills.\n6. Keyword Relevance.\n7. Profile Completeness.\n\nDisplay:\n\n* Overall Profile Quality Score.\n* Category-wise analysis.\n* Strengths.\n* Weak areas.\n* Missing information.\n* Improvement recommendations.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nKeep this score separate from the Resume Match Score.\n\nA LinkedIn profile quality score is not the same as a job-description compatibility score.\n\nDo not invent scores or display fake results.\n\nUse transparent backend logic for any numerical scoring.\n\n==================================================\n5. AI LINKEDIN HEADLINE GENERATOR\n=================================\n\nGenerate up to three headline suggestions.\n\nEach suggestion should:\n\n* Clearly communicate professional identity.\n* Highlight relevant skills.\n* Include relevant keywords.\n* Match the candidate\'s career direction.\n* Stay within LinkedIn\'s current headline character limit.\n\nAllow the user to:\n\n* Copy headline.\n* Edit headline.\n* Accept suggestion.\n* Reject suggestion.\n\n==================================================\n6. ABOUT SECTION OPTIMIZER\n==========================\n\nGenerate an improved About section.\n\nRequirements:\n\n* Professional introduction.\n* Key skills.\n* Relevant projects.\n* Education or experience.\n* Career interests.\n* Clear professional direction.\n\nAvoid generic AI-generated phrases.\n\nMake the writing sound natural and authentic.\n\nProvide different writing styles:\n\n* Professional.\n* Student / Fresher.\n* Technical.\n* Concise.\n\nAllow users to compare original and improved versions.\n\n==================================================\n7. EXPERIENCE AND PROJECT OPTIMIZER\n===================================\n\nImprove experience and project descriptions.\n\nUse:\n\n* Strong action verbs.\n* Clear sentences.\n* Relevant keywords.\n* Specific technical contributions.\n* Readable bullet points.\n\nDo not invent metrics or achievements.\n\nIf additional information is required, ask the candidate.\n\nDisplay:\n\nORIGINAL DESCRIPTION\nAI-IMPROVED DESCRIPTION\nREASON FOR IMPROVEMENT\nTRUTHGUARD STATUS\n\n==================================================\n8. SKILLS AND KEYWORD ANALYSIS\n==============================\n\nDisplay:\n\n* Existing skills.\n* Relevant skills already demonstrated.\n* Skills that need stronger evidence.\n* Missing or unmentioned job-related keywords.\n\nIf a target job description is supplied, compare profile information against it.\n\nUse the same EvidenceMap principles as Resume Architect.\n\nStatuses:\n\n* MATCHED.\n* PARTIALLY MATCHED.\n* NOT FOUND.\n\nNever claim that a user possesses a missing skill.\n\n==================================================\n9. TRUTHGUARD INTEGRATION\n=========================\n\nUse the existing TruthGuard system.\n\nValidate every AI-generated suggestion.\n\nStatuses:\n\nSUPPORTED:\nDirectly supported by candidate information.\n\nNEEDS CONFIRMATION:\nRequires user verification.\n\nUNSUPPORTED:\nNo evidence supports the statement.\n\nNever automatically publish or apply unsupported claims.\n\nThe user must approve every change.\n\n==================================================\n10. LINKEDIN PREVIEW\n====================\n\nCreate a LinkedIn-style profile preview.\n\nDisplay:\n\n* Name.\n* Headline.\n* About section.\n* Experience.\n* Education.\n* Projects.\n* Skills.\n* Certifications.\n\nAllow users to switch between:\n\nORIGINAL PROFILE\nOPTIMISED PROFILE\n\nThe preview must update when the user accepts or edits suggestions.\n\n==================================================\n11. SAVE AND EXPORT\n===================\n\nAllow users to:\n\n* Save profile drafts.\n* Save optimised versions.\n* View previous versions.\n* Compare original and optimised content.\n* Copy individual sections.\n* Copy the complete profile content.\n\nAdd a clear notice:\n\n\"Resume Architect prepares optimised LinkedIn content. Review and manually apply the approved changes to your LinkedIn profile.\"\n\nDo not claim to directly modify a LinkedIn account unless an authorised integration is actually implemented.\n\n==================================================\n12. RESUME ARCHITECT INTEGRATION\n================================\n\nConnect LinkedIn Optimizer with:\n\n* Candidate Profile.\n* AI Resume Studio.\n* Resume Editor.\n* My Resumes.\n* TruthGuard.\n\nUse shared candidate information wherever possible.\n\nIf a user updates their resume, allow them to refresh the imported LinkedIn information.\n\nDo not overwrite previously approved LinkedIn content automatically.\n\n==================================================\n13. DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS\n============================\n\n1. Inspect the existing project.\n2. Reuse the existing design system.\n3. Implement profile input.\n4. Implement resume import.\n5. Implement Gemini integration.\n6. Implement LinkedIn analysis.\n7. Implement headline generation.\n8. Implement About section optimisation.\n9. Implement experience and project optimisation.\n10. Integrate TruthGuard.\n11. Implement profile preview.\n12. Implement saving and version history.\n13. Test all features.\n14. Fix errors without breaking existing functionality.\n\nDo not create fake AI analysis or fabricated profile information.\n\nDo not stop after creating a visual mockup. Implement the working LinkedIn Profile Optimizer.\n\nWhen finished, explain which features are working and which require additional backend or external API configuration."
    }
  }
}
