  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Objective**\n\nI\'ve crafted a detailed candidate profile, which I believe is realistic and comprehensive. Now, I am focused on meticulously reviewing the user\'s specific requirements for the LinkedIn Profile Optimizer. I\'m carefully examining the precise specifications.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Focus**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the LinkedIn Profile Optimizer\'s core function: assisting individuals in showcasing their skills authentically. It will focus on helping students, freshers, and professionals present themselves effectively. I\'m prioritizing the use of genuine candidate information and ensuring the AI never fabricates any data. I\'ve begun to define the page title and subtitle.\n\n\n**Expanding the Scope**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed sections, including location, target job roles, headlines, and comprehensive \"About\" summaries. I\'m building out experience, education, and projects with specific fields for company, job titles, and dates, with bullet point support. Further, skills, certifications, and an option to import from Resume Architect are in progress. Finally, I\'m focusing on incorporating an AI analysis and scoring module.\n\n\n**Defining the Scoring Criteria**\n\nI\'ve established the detailed scoring system and its transparent breakdown. I am working on how I\'ll weigh different elements within the LinkedIn profile for evaluation. I\'m focusing on providing specific scores for headline quality, the \"About\" section, experience presentation, project impact, skills and keywords, keyword relevance, and overall profile completeness.\n\n\n**Refining the Evaluation**\n\nI\'m now distinguishing between LinkedIn profile optimization and job-specific ATS matching. My priority is enhancing profile effectiveness and recruiter visibility. I am working on how this distinction will affect the scoring system.\n\n\n**Defining Target Audiences**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the target audience profiles for the LinkedIn Profile Optimizer. I will ensure the system supports experienced professionals with authority, students and freshers, with a focus on highlighting education, projects, and ambition. I will also incorporate support for technical professionals, including developers. Finally, I will ensure a concise, high-impact presentation.\n\n**Adding User Interface Features**\n\nI am now adding the user interface features. I am prioritizing a side-by-side or tabbed diff feature that will compare the current and optimized profiles, with key improvements highlighted. There will be one-click accept, edit, or reject functionality.\n\n**Focusing on Bullet Optimization**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on optimizing experience and project bullet points, I am working on bullet point enhancement using the XYZ/STAR impact formula (Accomplished [X], measured by [Y], by doing [Z]). I\'ve decided to add a TruthGuard verification badge on each bullet point, using SUPPORTED, NEEDS CONFIRMATION, and NEVER FABRICATE statuses. One-click options for accepting, editing, and rejecting the changes will be available. Finally, I will also begin a Skills & Keyword Analysis.\n\n\n**Analyzing Keyword Relevance**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a keyword relevance analysis. I am comparing extracted skills to high-demand keywords and providing evidence statuses: MATCHED, PARTIALLY MATCHED, and RECOMMENDED TO ADD. I am also highlighting missing keywords that the candidate can claim based on their background.\n\n**Generating a Preview**\n\nI\'m now creating an interactive LinkedIn-style profile card preview. It includes all the standard profile elements like banner, avatar, name, and various sections. I\'m adding a toggle between the original and optimized versions, and it will dynamically update as the user accepts suggestions.\n\n**Adding Save & Export Functions**\n\nI\'m also adding Save & Export functionality. I am including the option to save drafts and revisions. I am also adding clipboard copy for individual sections and a button to copy all optimized content, along with a clear disclaimer notice for the user.\n\n\n**Structuring the Data**\n\nI\'m now structuring the core data models within `src/types/linkedin.ts`, beginning with the `LinkedInProfileData`. This includes defining the types for `personalInfo`, `headline`, `about`, `experience`, `education`, `projects`, `skills`, and `certifications`. Further, I\'m working to define types for `HeadlineSuggestion` and `AboutOptimization`, including the style.\n\n\n**Refining the Data Models**\n\nI\'m now refining the data models further to support new features and analysis components. I\'ve defined `ExperienceBulletOptimization` and `ProjectBulletOptimization` to include truth guard statuses and applied formulas. Also, I\'ve defined `SkillEvidenceItem` with matching statuses, source evidence, and relevance notes. Lastly, I\'ve defined the structure for `LinkedInQualityScoreCategory` and overall `LinkedInAnalysis`.\n\n\n**Defining the Analysis**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the creation of the core analysis and scoring mechanisms. I\'ve designed the detailed structure of the `LinkedInAnalysis` object, incorporating the `overallScore`, `scoreGrade`, and breakdowns across various categories like Headline, \"About,\" Experience, Skills, and Overall Completeness. The structure includes both strengths and weak areas, providing actionable recommendations. The analysis will integrate specific suggestions for headlines and \"About\" sections. I\'ve also integrated experience and project optimizations that include truth guard statuses and applied formulas and skill evidence items. Finally, I\'ve integrated saved drafts and revisions functionality. I will also incorporate a saved draft mechanism with revisions.\n\n\n**Implementing the Core Logic**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the core logic of the analysis and scoring system. I am integrating the defined APIs and service layer, including endpoints for analysis, headline generation, and \"About\" section optimization. I\'m building out the frontend service with methods for analyzing LinkedIn profiles, saving/retrieving drafts, importing from resumes, and providing default sample profiles. My priority is to create the essential UI components within the `src/components/linkedin/` directory, especially the `LinkedInView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing the Layout**\n\nI am now designing the layout to maximize usability and clearly present the information. I am working on a split layout with an input form on the left and analysis/preview on the right. The input form will be organized into clean tabs, including personal info, headline/about, experience, education, projects, skills, and certifications. I\'m focusing on making the input fields visually clear.\n\n\n**Developing the Presentation**\n\nI\'m now focused on the final presentation to the user, particularly integrating all the optimization components into the interactive LinkedIn preview. I\'ve integrated TruthGuard badges and accept/edit buttons for experience bullets, along with the Skills & Keyword EvidenceMap. I\'m building an authentic LinkedIn desktop profile card preview. The preview now incorporates a toggle for real-time comparison. I\'m building out copy/export functionality.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_801028"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * Resume Architect \342\200\224 LinkedIn Profile Optimizer Types\\n * Decoupled, production-ready types for LinkedIn analysis, scoring, and optimization.\\n */\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInPersonalInfo {\\n  fullName: string;\\n  currentTitleOrStatus: string;\\n  location: string;\\n  targetRole: string;\\n  targetIndustry: string;\\n  openToWork: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInExperienceItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  company: string;\\n  jobTitle: string;\\n  location?: string;\\n  startDate: string;\\n  endDate: string;\\n  isCurrent: boolean;\\n  bullets: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInEducationItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  degree: string;\\n  institution: string;\\n  graduationYear: string;\\n  details: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInProjectItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  tech: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  bullets: string[];\\n  link?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInCertificationItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  issuer: string;\\n  year?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInProfileData {\\n  personalInfo: LinkedInPersonalInfo;\\n  headline: string;\\n  about: string;\\n  experience: LinkedInExperienceItem[];\\n  education: LinkedInEducationItem[];\\n  projects: LinkedInProjectItem[];\\n  skills: {\\n    technical: string[];\\n    softAndTools: string[];\\n  };\\n  certifications: LinkedInCertificationItem[];\\n}\\n\\nexport type HeadlineStyleType = \'value-prop\' | \'keyword-dense\' | \'growth-impact\';\\n\\nexport interface HeadlineSuggestion {\\n  id: string;\\n  type: HeadlineStyleType;\\n  label: string;\\n  text: string;\\n  charCount: number;\\n  keywordsIncluded: string[];\\n  rationale: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type AboutStyleType = \'professional\' | \'fresher\' | \'technical\' | \'concise\';\\n\\nexport interface AboutOptimization {\\n  style: AboutStyleType;\\n  styleLabel: string;\\n  text: string;\\n  keyImprovements: string[];\\n  callToAction: string;\\n  wordCount: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport type TruthGuardStatus = \'SUPPORTED\' | \'NEEDS CONFIRMATION\' | \'UNSUPPORTED\';\\n\\nexport interface ExperienceBulletOptimization {\\n  id: string;\\n  experienceId: string;\\n  company: string;\\n  jobTitle: string;\\n  originalBullet: string;\\n  optimizedBullet: string;\\n  truthGuardStatus: TruthGuardStatus;\\n  confirmationNote?: string;\\n  appliedFormula: \'XYZ\' | \'STAR\';\\n  accepted?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ProjectBulletOptimization {\\n  id: string;\\n  projectId: string;\\n  projectTitle: string;\\n  originalBullet: string;\\n  optimizedBullet: string;\\n  truthGuardStatus: TruthGuardStatus;\\n  confirmationNote?: string;\\n  accepted?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport type EvidenceStatus = \'MATCHED\' | \'PARTIALLY MATCHED\' | \'RECOMMENDED_TO_ADD\';\\n\\nexport interface SkillEvidenceItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  skill: string;\\n  category: \'Technical\' | \'Soft & Domain\' | \'Industry Keyword\';\\n  status: EvidenceStatus;\\n  sourceEvidence: string;\\n  relevanceNote: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type LinkedInScoreCategoryId =\\n  | \'headline\'\\n  | \'about\'\\n  | \'experience\'\\n  | \'projects\'\\n  | \'skills\'\\n  | \'keywords\'\\n  | \'completeness\';\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInQualityScoreCategory {\\n  id: LinkedInScoreCategoryId;\\n  name: string;\\n  score: number; // 0 - 100\\n  weight: number; // e.g. 0.15\\n  status: \'optimal\' | \'moderate\' | \'action-required\';\\n  feedback: string;\\n  metrics: {\\n    value: string;\\n    target: string;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInAnalysisResult {\\n  id: string;\\n  overallScore: number; // 0 - 100\\n  scoreGrade: \'Executive All-Star\' | \'Strong Contender\' | \'Developing\' | \'Needs Optimization\';\\n  categories: LinkedInQualityScoreCategory[];\\n  strengths: string[];\\n  weakAreas: string[];\\n  recommendations: string[];\\n  headlineSuggestions: HeadlineSuggestion[];\\n  aboutOptimizations: Record<AboutStyleType, AboutOptimization>;\\n  experienceOptimizations: ExperienceBulletOptimization[];\\n  projectOptimizations: ProjectBulletOptimization[];\\n  skillEvidence: SkillEvidenceItem[];\\n  analyzedAt: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LinkedInSavedDraft {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  savedAt: string;\\n  profileData: LinkedInProfileData;\\n  score?: number;\\n  scoreGrade?: string;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Define comprehensive TypeScript types for LinkedIn Profile Optimizer\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/linkedin.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing types\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create LinkedIn types file\"}"
