  planner_response {
    response: "The **AI-powered LinkedIn Profile Optimizer** has been built for Resume Architect, adhering strictly to the forest-green and warm off-white design system, maintaining zero fabrication discipline, and integrating directly with existing resumes.\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Two-Panel Workspace Layout**:\n   - **Page Title**: `LinkedIn Profile Optimizer`\n   - **Subtitle**: `Build a stronger professional identity and showcase your skills with confidence.`\n   - **Left Panel (Profile Information Form)**:\n     - **Option A (Manual Input)**: Tabbed input for Personal Information (with `#OpenToWork` toggle), Headline (with char counter), About Section (with word counter), Work Experience (company, title, dates, dynamic bullets), Education, Projects, Technical & Soft Skills, and Certifications.\n     - **Option B (Resume Architect Import)**: Direct 1-click import from any saved resume in Resume Architect with field pre-population and full editability.\n     - **Testing Presets**: One-click loaders for *Experienced Engineer* and *CS Student / Fresher*.\n\n2. **LinkedIn Profile Quality Score Engine (0\342\200\223100)**:\n   - Completely independent from the job-specific ATS resume match score; calibrated for profile discoverability and recruiter search visibility.\n   - Transparent 7-dimension weighted breakdown:\n     - **Headline Quality** (15%)\n     - **About Section Narrative** (20%)\n     - **Experience Presentation** (20%)\n     - **Project Impact & Real-World Utility** (15%)\n     - **Technical & Soft Skills Coverage** (10%)\n     - **Keyword Relevance & Algorithmic Discovery** (10%)\n     - **Profile Completeness** (10%)\n   - Shows overall score, grade (e.g. *Executive All-Star*, *Strong Contender*), category progress bars, and target metrics.\n\n3. **AI Headline Generator**:\n   - Generates 3 recruiter-calibrated headline options:\n     - **Role & Value Proposition** (e.g., role + primary technology + commercial impact)\n     - **Recruiter Search-Optimized** (high-frequency keyword density for LinkedIn search algorithms)\n     - **Growth & Impact Focused** (engineering philosophy, code craft, and business outcomes)\n   - Features real-time character counters strictly tracking LinkedIn\'s 220-character limit, one-click copy, and an **\"Accept as Headline\"** action that updates the profile live.\n\n4. **About Section Optimizer (4 Tailored Narrative Styles)**:\n   - **Professional & Authoritative**: 3-paragraph executive narrative with tech stack positioning and networking call-to-action.\n   - **Student / Fresher Friendly**: Emphasizes project deliverables, learning agility, academic achievements, and junior career ambition.\n   - **Technical & Architecture Focused**: Scannable bulleted overview of systems, protocols, and tooling for hiring managers.\n   - **Concise & Punchy**: Ultra-scannable under-60-word mobile-optimized summary.\n   - Side-by-side comparison of current bio vs. optimized version, key improvement highlights, and one-click accept.\n\n5. **Experience & Project Bullet Optimizer (TruthGuard Grounded)**:\n   - Reformats bullet points using the **XYZ / STAR impact formula** (*Accomplished [X], measured by [Y], by doing [Z]*).\n   - Validates every bullet with **TruthGuard status badges**:\n     - `SUPPORTED`: Fully verified by the candidate\'s raw data.\n     - `NEEDS CONFIRMATION`: Highlights metrics or scale figures that the user should confirm without inventing numbers.\n   - One-click copy or apply to profile.\n\n6. **Skills & Keyword EvidenceMap**:\n   - Verifies candidate skills against market expectations for the target role with `MATCHED`, `PARTIALLY MATCHED`, and `RECOMMENDED_TO_ADD` statuses, citing genuine candidate evidence.\n\n7. **Interactive LinkedIn Profile Preview**:\n   - Authentic LinkedIn profile card featuring cover banner, initials avatar, name, headline, location, contact badge, About section, Experience timeline, Education, Projects, and Skill chips.\n   - Live **\"Original Profile\" vs. \"Optimised Profile\"** toggle that dynamically reflects accepted headline, about, and bullet improvements in real time.\n\n8. **Save & Export Modal**:\n   - Section-by-section clipboard copy (Headline, About, Experience descriptions, Skills).\n   - Single-click **\"Copy All Optimised Content\"** button with formatted markdown.\n   - Local drafts and revision history manager with restore capability.\n   - Explicit required disclaimer: *\"Resume Architect prepares optimised LinkedIn content. Review and manually apply the approved changes to your LinkedIn profile.\"*"
    thinking: "**Confirming Key Requirements**\n\nI\'ve just finished verifying that I\'ve accurately captured and implemented the user\'s initial requirements. I\'ve confirmed I am only building the LinkedIn Profile Optimizer in this phase, and that the page title and subtitle are as specified. Now I am planning to move on to incorporating the specified content blocks and their respective functionalities.\n\n\n**Defining Functional Elements**\n\nI\'ve completed defining the application\'s major sections: the left panel for LinkedIn profile data input and the right for AI analysis. I\'ve also implemented both input options: manual entry and resume import. Additionally, I\'ve defined the AI\'s LinkedIn profile analysis and scoring process, along with its headline generator, which offers multiple options with a character count, and copy/edit/accept functionality. Now, I am working on the about section optimizer and its distinct writing styles.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **AI-powered LinkedIn Profile Optimizer** has been built for Resume Architect, adhering strictly to the forest-green and warm off-white design system, maintaining zero fabrication discipline, and integrating directly with existing resumes.\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Two-Panel Workspace Layout**:\n   - **Page Title**: `LinkedIn Profile Optimizer`\n   - **Subtitle**: `Build a stronger professional identity and showcase your skills with confidence.`\n   - **Left Panel (Profile Information Form)**:\n     - **Option A (Manual Input)**: Tabbed input for Personal Information (with `#OpenToWork` toggle), Headline (with char counter), About Section (with word counter), Work Experience (company, title, dates, dynamic bullets), Education, Projects, Technical & Soft Skills, and Certifications.\n     - **Option B (Resume Architect Import)**: Direct 1-click import from any saved resume in Resume Architect with field pre-population and full editability.\n     - **Testing Presets**: One-click loaders for *Experienced Engineer* and *CS Student / Fresher*.\n\n2. **LinkedIn Profile Quality Score Engine (0\342\200\223100)**:\n   - Completely independent from the job-specific ATS resume match score; calibrated for profile discoverability and recruiter search visibility.\n   - Transparent 7-dimension weighted breakdown:\n     - **Headline Quality** (15%)\n     - **About Section Narrative** (20%)\n     - **Experience Presentation** (20%)\n     - **Project Impact & Real-World Utility** (15%)\n     - **Technical & Soft Skills Coverage** (10%)\n     - **Keyword Relevance & Algorithmic Discovery** (10%)\n     - **Profile Completeness** (10%)\n   - Shows overall score, grade (e.g. *Executive All-Star*, *Strong Contender*), category progress bars, and target metrics.\n\n3. **AI Headline Generator**:\n   - Generates 3 recruiter-calibrated headline options:\n     - **Role & Value Proposition** (e.g., role + primary technology + commercial impact)\n     - **Recruiter Search-Optimized** (high-frequency keyword density for LinkedIn search algorithms)\n     - **Growth & Impact Focused** (engineering philosophy, code craft, and business outcomes)\n   - Features real-time character counters strictly tracking LinkedIn\'s 220-character limit, one-click copy, and an **\"Accept as Headline\"** action that updates the profile live.\n\n4. **About Section Optimizer (4 Tailored Narrative Styles)**:\n   - **Professional & Authoritative**: 3-paragraph executive narrative with tech stack positioning and networking call-to-action.\n   - **Student / Fresher Friendly**: Emphasizes project deliverables, learning agility, academic achievements, and junior career ambition.\n   - **Technical & Architecture Focused**: Scannable bulleted overview of systems, protocols, and tooling for hiring managers.\n   - **Concise & Punchy**: Ultra-scannable under-60-word mobile-optimized summary.\n   - Side-by-side comparison of current bio vs. optimized version, key improvement highlights, and one-click accept.\n\n5. **Experience & Project Bullet Optimizer (TruthGuard Grounded)**:\n   - Reformats bullet points using the **XYZ / STAR impact formula** (*Accomplished [X], measured by [Y], by doing [Z]*).\n   - Validates every bullet with **TruthGuard status badges**:\n     - `SUPPORTED`: Fully verified by the candidate\'s raw data.\n     - `NEEDS CONFIRMATION`: Highlights metrics or scale figures that the user should confirm without inventing numbers.\n   - One-click copy or apply to profile.\n\n6. **Skills & Keyword EvidenceMap**:\n   - Verifies candidate skills against market expectations for the target role with `MATCHED`, `PARTIALLY MATCHED`, and `RECOMMENDED_TO_ADD` statuses, citing genuine candidate evidence.\n\n7. **Interactive LinkedIn Profile Preview**:\n   - Authentic LinkedIn profile card featuring cover banner, initials avatar, name, headline, location, contact badge, About section, Experience timeline, Education, Projects, and Skill chips.\n   - Live **\"Original Profile\" vs. \"Optimised Profile\"** toggle that dynamically reflects accepted headline, about, and bullet improvements in real time.\n\n8. **Save & Export Modal**:\n   - Section-by-section clipboard copy (Headline, About, Experience descriptions, Skills).\n   - Single-click **\"Copy All Optimised Content\"** button with formatted markdown.\n   - Local drafts and revision history manager with restore capability.\n   - Explicit required disclaimer: *\"Resume Architect prepares optimised LinkedIn content. Review and manually apply the approved changes to your LinkedIn profile.\"*"
