  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue developing the existing Resume Architect project.\n\nPROJECT: RESUME ARCHITECT\n\nTAGLINE: Don\'t just match the job. Prove your fit.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not create a new project.\nDo not redesign existing UI.\nDo not delete existing working features.\nInspect the complete existing codebase before making changes.\n\nThe objective is to integrate every existing feature into one functional application.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. TECHNOLOGY ARCHITECTURE\n   ==================================================\n\nFRONTEND:\n\n* React.js\n* Vite\n* JavaScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* React Router\n\nBACKEND:\n\n* Python\n* FastAPI\n* REST APIs\n\nDATABASE:\n\n* SQLite\n* SQLAlchemy ORM\n\nAI:\n\n* Google Gemini API.\n\nDOCUMENT PROCESSING:\n\n* PyMuPDF for PDF extraction.\n* python-docx for DOCX processing.\n* Playwright for PDF generation.\n\nMaintain a clean separation between frontend, backend, AI services and database operations.\n\n==================================================\n2. CENTRAL BACKEND ARCHITECTURE\n===============================\n\nCreate a backend structure similar to:\n\nbackend/\napp/\nmain.py\n\n```\n    api/\n        auth.py\n        resumes.py\n        analysis.py\n        editor.py\n        linkedin.py\n\n    core/\n        config.py\n        security.py\n\n    database/\n        connection.py\n        models.py\n\n    services/\n        gemini_service.py\n        resume_parser.py\n        jd_parser.py\n        score_engine.py\n        evidence_map.py\n        truthguard.py\n        resume_service.py\n        linkedin_service.py\n        export_service.py\n\n    schemas/\n        resume_schema.py\n        analysis_schema.py\n        linkedin_schema.py\n\nrequirements.txt\n.env.example\n```\n\nAdjust the structure if necessary, but maintain modularity.\n\n==================================================\n3. GEMINI AI CENTRAL SERVICE\n============================\n\nCreate one central Gemini AI service.\n\nAll AI-related features must use this service instead of implementing separate Gemini connections throughout the application.\n\nSupport these operations:\n\nA. CREATE_RESUME\nGenerate a professional resume using actual candidate information.\n\nB. REVIEW_RESUME\nAnalyse the uploaded resume against a job description.\n\nC. IMPROVE_RESUME\nGenerate truthful improvements based on identified weaknesses.\n\nD. OPTIMIZE_LINKEDIN\nImprove LinkedIn headline, About, experience, projects and skills.\n\nE. TRUTHGUARD_VALIDATE\nValidate whether AI suggestions are supported by candidate information.\n\nUse structured JSON outputs.\n\nValidate all responses before passing them to other services.\n\nHandle:\n\n* API failures.\n* Invalid JSON.\n* Empty responses.\n* Rate limits.\n* Model unavailability.\n* Network errors.\n\nNever expose the Gemini API key in frontend code.\n\nRead the API key from backend environment variables.\n\nUse the currently available Gemini model configured through environment variables. Do not hardcode an outdated model name.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESUME SCORE ENGINE\n======================\n\nThis is the central intelligence of Resume Architect.\n\nImplement the score engine as an independent Python module.\n\nIt must not depend on Gemini for numerical score calculation.\n\nUse these weights:\n\n1. Technical Skills Alignment: 30%.\n2. Keyword Alignment: 20%.\n3. Project Relevance: 20%.\n4. Experience Relevance: 15%.\n5. Education Relevance: 5%.\n6. Formatting and Readability: 10%.\n\nFormula:\n\nFinal Score =\n(Skills \303\227 0.30) +\n(Keywords \303\227 0.20) +\n(Projects \303\227 0.20) +\n(Experience \303\227 0.15) +\n(Education \303\227 0.05) +\n(Formatting \303\227 0.10)\n\nEvery category score must be between 0 and 100.\n\nUse deterministic calculations wherever possible.\n\nGemini can help identify semantic relationships and evidence, but the backend must validate the results and calculate the final score.\n\nAvoid double-counting requirements.\n\nHandle non-applicable categories transparently using a documented weight adjustment.\n\nReturn:\n\n* Overall score.\n* Category scores.\n* Matched requirements.\n* Partially matched requirements.\n* Unmentioned requirements.\n* Improvement recommendations.\n* Scoring explanation.\n\nThe same input must produce consistent results.\n\n==================================================\n5. EVIDENCEMAP INTEGRATION\n==========================\n\nIntegrate EvidenceMap into the analysis workflow.\n\nFor every important job requirement, identify:\n\n* Requirement name.\n* Supporting resume evidence.\n* Evidence location.\n* Match status.\n* Explanation.\n\nStatuses:\n\nMATCHED\nPARTIALLY MATCHED\nNOT FOUND\n\nDo not interpret NOT FOUND as proof that the candidate lacks the skill.\n\n==================================================\n6. TRUTHGUARD INTEGRATION\n=========================\n\nIntegrate TruthGuard into every AI improvement workflow.\n\nValidate:\n\n* Skills.\n* Experience.\n* Achievements.\n* Metrics.\n* Project contributions.\n* Technologies.\n* Certifications.\n* Qualifications.\n\nStatuses:\n\nSUPPORTED\nNEEDS_CONFIRMATION\nUNSUPPORTED\n\nUnsupported claims must never be automatically inserted into the final resume.\n\nRequire user approval for changes.\n\n==================================================\n7. DATABASE INTEGRATION\n=======================\n\nCreate SQLite database models for:\n\nUSER:\n\n* ID.\n* Name.\n* Email.\n* Password hash.\n* Created date.\n\nCANDIDATE PROFILE:\n\n* User ID.\n* Personal details.\n* Education.\n* Skills.\n* Projects.\n* Experience.\n* Certifications.\n\nRESUME:\n\n* Resume ID.\n* User ID.\n* Resume title.\n* Target role.\n* Structured resume data.\n* Creation date.\n* Updated date.\n\nRESUME VERSION:\n\n* Version ID.\n* Resume ID.\n* Version number.\n* Resume data snapshot.\n* Created date.\n\nRESUME ANALYSIS:\n\n* Analysis ID.\n* Resume version ID.\n* Target job description.\n* Overall score.\n* Category scores.\n* EvidenceMap results.\n* Recommendations.\n* Analysis date.\n\nLINKEDIN PROFILE:\n\n* Profile ID.\n* User ID.\n* Profile data.\n* Optimised content.\n* Updated date.\n\nACTIVITY:\n\n* Activity ID.\n* User ID.\n* Activity type.\n* Description.\n* Timestamp.\n\nEnsure proper database relationships.\n\nNever overwrite previous resume versions unintentionally.\n\n==================================================\n8. API ENDPOINTS\n================\n\nImplement REST endpoints.\n\nAUTHENTICATION:\nPOST /api/auth/signup\nPOST /api/auth/login\nGET /api/auth/me\n\nRESUMES:\nPOST /api/resumes\nGET /api/resumes\nGET /api/resumes/{id}\nPUT /api/resumes/{id}\nDELETE /api/resumes/{id}\n\nVERSIONS:\nPOST /api/resumes/{id}/versions\nGET /api/resumes/{id}/versions\n\nANALYSIS:\nPOST /api/analysis/upload\nPOST /api/analysis/review\nGET /api/analysis/{id}\n\nAI IMPROVEMENT:\nPOST /api/resumes/{id}/improve\n\nEDITOR:\nPUT /api/resumes/{id}/content\n\nEXPORT:\nGET /api/resumes/{id}/export/pdf\nGET /api/resumes/{id}/export/docx\n\nLINKEDIN:\nPOST /api/linkedin/analyze\nPOST /api/linkedin/optimize\nGET /api/linkedin/profile\nPUT /api/linkedin/profile\n\nModify endpoint structures where necessary to support the existing frontend.\n\n==================================================\n9. FRONTEND INTEGRATION\n=======================\n\nConnect every existing page to the backend.\n\nAI RESUME STUDIO:\n\n* Save candidate information.\n* Generate resumes using Gemini.\n* Save generated versions.\n\nRESUME REVIEWER:\n\n* Upload PDF/DOCX.\n* Extract text.\n* Submit resume and job description.\n* Display actual score engine results.\n* Display EvidenceMap.\n* Display skill gaps.\n\nRESUME EDITOR:\n\n* Load saved resume.\n* Save edits.\n* Create versions.\n* Reanalyse updated content.\n* Export PDF/DOCX.\n\nLINKEDIN OPTIMIZER:\n\n* Import information from saved resumes.\n* Analyse profile information.\n* Generate optimised content.\n* Save approved versions.\n\nDASHBOARD:\n\n* Display saved resumes.\n* Display latest genuine analysis scores.\n* Display recent activities.\n\nRemove temporary mock data from production workflows.\n\nIf a feature is not connected yet, display a clear development status rather than fake success.\n\n==================================================\n10. SECURITY\n============\n\nImplement:\n\n* Password hashing.\n* Token-based authentication.\n* Protected backend routes.\n* Input validation.\n* File type validation.\n* File size limits.\n* Safe file handling.\n* User-specific data access.\n* Environment variable configuration.\n\nA user must never be able to access another user\'s resumes or analysis results.\n\nDo not store plaintext passwords.\n\nDo not expose API keys or sensitive configuration in frontend code.\n\n==================================================\n11. ERROR HANDLING\n==================\n\nProvide proper error messages for:\n\n* Invalid login.\n* Invalid file.\n* Failed PDF extraction.\n* Failed DOCX extraction.\n* Empty job description.\n* Invalid job URL.\n* Gemini API failure.\n* Database errors.\n* Failed PDF/DOCX export.\n* Network errors.\n\nDo not silently fail.\n\n==================================================\n12. TESTING\n===========\n\nTest the complete application.\n\nTest these user journeys:\n\nJOURNEY 1:\nSignup \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Dashboard.\n\nJOURNEY 2:\nDashboard \342\206\222 Create Resume \342\206\222 Generate with Gemini \342\206\222 Save Resume \342\206\222 Open Editor.\n\nJOURNEY 3:\nUpload Resume \342\206\222 Add Job Description \342\206\222 Analyse \342\206\222 Receive Score \342\206\222 View EvidenceMap.\n\nJOURNEY 4:\nAnalyse Resume \342\206\222 Improve with AI \342\206\222 TruthGuard Validation \342\206\222 Approve Changes \342\206\222 Save New Version.\n\nJOURNEY 5:\nOpen Editor \342\206\222 Edit Resume \342\206\222 Reanalyse \342\206\222 Download PDF/DOCX.\n\nJOURNEY 6:\nOpen LinkedIn Optimizer \342\206\222 Import Resume \342\206\222 Optimise Profile \342\206\222 Save Changes.\n\nVerify that all user data is saved correctly.\n\n==================================================\n13. FINAL DEVELOPMENT RULES\n===========================\n\n1. Inspect the complete existing application.\n2. Identify incomplete and duplicated implementations.\n3. Reuse existing code.\n4. Implement the backend.\n5. Connect Gemini.\n6. Connect SQLite.\n7. Connect the Resume Score Engine.\n8. Integrate EvidenceMap and TruthGuard.\n9. Connect every frontend workflow.\n10. Test all six user journeys.\n11. Fix all critical errors.\n12. Preserve the existing UI.\n\nDo not replace working components unnecessarily.\n\nDo not generate fake analysis results.\n\nDo not claim a feature is working unless it has actually been tested.\n\nDo not stop after creating files or a development plan.\n\nImplement the integration and run the application.\n\nAt the end, provide:\n\n* Backend setup instructions.\n* Frontend setup instructions.\n* Required environment variables.\n* Gemini API configuration steps.\n* Database setup instructions.\n* List of completed features.\n* List of remaining issues."
    items {
      text: "Continue developing the existing Resume Architect project.\n\nPROJECT: RESUME ARCHITECT\n\nTAGLINE: Don\'t just match the job. Prove your fit.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not create a new project.\nDo not redesign existing UI.\nDo not delete existing working features.\nInspect the complete existing codebase before making changes.\n\nThe objective is to integrate every existing feature into one functional application.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. TECHNOLOGY ARCHITECTURE\n   ==================================================\n\nFRONTEND:\n\n* React.js\n* Vite\n* JavaScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* React Router\n\nBACKEND:\n\n* Python\n* FastAPI\n* REST APIs\n\nDATABASE:\n\n* SQLite\n* SQLAlchemy ORM\n\nAI:\n\n* Google Gemini API.\n\nDOCUMENT PROCESSING:\n\n* PyMuPDF for PDF extraction.\n* python-docx for DOCX processing.\n* Playwright for PDF generation.\n\nMaintain a clean separation between frontend, backend, AI services and database operations.\n\n==================================================\n2. CENTRAL BACKEND ARCHITECTURE\n===============================\n\nCreate a backend structure similar to:\n\nbackend/\napp/\nmain.py\n\n```\n    api/\n        auth.py\n        resumes.py\n        analysis.py\n        editor.py\n        linkedin.py\n\n    core/\n        config.py\n        security.py\n\n    database/\n        connection.py\n        models.py\n\n    services/\n        gemini_service.py\n        resume_parser.py\n        jd_parser.py\n        score_engine.py\n        evidence_map.py\n        truthguard.py\n        resume_service.py\n        linkedin_service.py\n        export_service.py\n\n    schemas/\n        resume_schema.py\n        analysis_schema.py\n        linkedin_schema.py\n\nrequirements.txt\n.env.example\n```\n\nAdjust the structure if necessary, but maintain modularity.\n\n==================================================\n3. GEMINI AI CENTRAL SERVICE\n============================\n\nCreate one central Gemini AI service.\n\nAll AI-related features must use this service instead of implementing separate Gemini connections throughout the application.\n\nSupport these operations:\n\nA. CREATE_RESUME\nGenerate a professional resume using actual candidate information.\n\nB. REVIEW_RESUME\nAnalyse the uploaded resume against a job description.\n\nC. IMPROVE_RESUME\nGenerate truthful improvements based on identified weaknesses.\n\nD. OPTIMIZE_LINKEDIN\nImprove LinkedIn headline, About, experience, projects and skills.\n\nE. TRUTHGUARD_VALIDATE\nValidate whether AI suggestions are supported by candidate information.\n\nUse structured JSON outputs.\n\nValidate all responses before passing them to other services.\n\nHandle:\n\n* API failures.\n* Invalid JSON.\n* Empty responses.\n* Rate limits.\n* Model unavailability.\n* Network errors.\n\nNever expose the Gemini API key in frontend code.\n\nRead the API key from backend environment variables.\n\nUse the currently available Gemini model configured through environment variables. Do not hardcode an outdated model name.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESUME SCORE ENGINE\n======================\n\nThis is the central intelligence of Resume Architect.\n\nImplement the score engine as an independent Python module.\n\nIt must not depend on Gemini for numerical score calculation.\n\nUse these weights:\n\n1. Technical Skills Alignment: 30%.\n2. Keyword Alignment: 20%.\n3. Project Relevance: 20%.\n4. Experience Relevance: 15%.\n5. Education Relevance: 5%.\n6. Formatting and Readability: 10%.\n\nFormula:\n\nFinal Score =\n(Skills \303\227 0.30) +\n(Keywords \303\227 0.20) +\n(Projects \303\227 0.20) +\n(Experience \303\227 0.15) +\n(Education \303\227 0.05) +\n(Formatting \303\227 0.10)\n\nEvery category score must be between 0 and 100.\n\nUse deterministic calculations wherever possible.\n\nGemini can help identify semantic relationships and evidence, but the backend must validate the results and calculate the final score.\n\nAvoid double-counting requirements.\n\nHandle non-applicable categories transparently using a documented weight adjustment.\n\nReturn:\n\n* Overall score.\n* Category scores.\n* Matched requirements.\n* Partially matched requirements.\n* Unmentioned requirements.\n* Improvement recommendations.\n* Scoring explanation.\n\nThe same input must produce consistent results.\n\n==================================================\n5. EVIDENCEMAP INTEGRATION\n==========================\n\nIntegrate EvidenceMap into the analysis workflow.\n\nFor every important job requirement, identify:\n\n* Requirement name.\n* Supporting resume evidence.\n* Evidence location.\n* Match status.\n* Explanation.\n\nStatuses:\n\nMATCHED\nPARTIALLY MATCHED\nNOT FOUND\n\nDo not interpret NOT FOUND as proof that the candidate lacks the skill.\n\n==================================================\n6. TRUTHGUARD INTEGRATION\n=========================\n\nIntegrate TruthGuard into every AI improvement workflow.\n\nValidate:\n\n* Skills.\n* Experience.\n* Achievements.\n* Metrics.\n* Project contributions.\n* Technologies.\n* Certifications.\n* Qualifications.\n\nStatuses:\n\nSUPPORTED\nNEEDS_CONFIRMATION\nUNSUPPORTED\n\nUnsupported claims must never be automatically inserted into the final resume.\n\nRequire user approval for changes.\n\n==================================================\n7. DATABASE INTEGRATION\n=======================\n\nCreate SQLite database models for:\n\nUSER:\n\n* ID.\n* Name.\n* Email.\n* Password hash.\n* Created date.\n\nCANDIDATE PROFILE:\n\n* User ID.\n* Personal details.\n* Education.\n* Skills.\n* Projects.\n* Experience.\n* Certifications.\n\nRESUME:\n\n* Resume ID.\n* User ID.\n* Resume title.\n* Target role.\n* Structured resume data.\n* Creation date.\n* Updated date.\n\nRESUME VERSION:\n\n* Version ID.\n* Resume ID.\n* Version number.\n* Resume data snapshot.\n* Created date.\n\nRESUME ANALYSIS:\n\n* Analysis ID.\n* Resume version ID.\n* Target job description.\n* Overall score.\n* Category scores.\n* EvidenceMap results.\n* Recommendations.\n* Analysis date.\n\nLINKEDIN PROFILE:\n\n* Profile ID.\n* User ID.\n* Profile data.\n* Optimised content.\n* Updated date.\n\nACTIVITY:\n\n* Activity ID.\n* User ID.\n* Activity type.\n* Description.\n* Timestamp.\n\nEnsure proper database relationships.\n\nNever overwrite previous resume versions unintentionally.\n\n==================================================\n8. API ENDPOINTS\n================\n\nImplement REST endpoints.\n\nAUTHENTICATION:\nPOST /api/auth/signup\nPOST /api/auth/login\nGET /api/auth/me\n\nRESUMES:\nPOST /api/resumes\nGET /api/resumes\nGET /api/resumes/{id}\nPUT /api/resumes/{id}\nDELETE /api/resumes/{id}\n\nVERSIONS:\nPOST /api/resumes/{id}/versions\nGET /api/resumes/{id}/versions\n\nANALYSIS:\nPOST /api/analysis/upload\nPOST /api/analysis/review\nGET /api/analysis/{id}\n\nAI IMPROVEMENT:\nPOST /api/resumes/{id}/improve\n\nEDITOR:\nPUT /api/resumes/{id}/content\n\nEXPORT:\nGET /api/resumes/{id}/export/pdf\nGET /api/resumes/{id}/export/docx\n\nLINKEDIN:\nPOST /api/linkedin/analyze\nPOST /api/linkedin/optimize\nGET /api/linkedin/profile\nPUT /api/linkedin/profile\n\nModify endpoint structures where necessary to support the existing frontend.\n\n==================================================\n9. FRONTEND INTEGRATION\n=======================\n\nConnect every existing page to the backend.\n\nAI RESUME STUDIO:\n\n* Save candidate information.\n* Generate resumes using Gemini.\n* Save generated versions.\n\nRESUME REVIEWER:\n\n* Upload PDF/DOCX.\n* Extract text.\n* Submit resume and job description.\n* Display actual score engine results.\n* Display EvidenceMap.\n* Display skill gaps.\n\nRESUME EDITOR:\n\n* Load saved resume.\n* Save edits.\n* Create versions.\n* Reanalyse updated content.\n* Export PDF/DOCX.\n\nLINKEDIN OPTIMIZER:\n\n* Import information from saved resumes.\n* Analyse profile information.\n* Generate optimised content.\n* Save approved versions.\n\nDASHBOARD:\n\n* Display saved resumes.\n* Display latest genuine analysis scores.\n* Display recent activities.\n\nRemove temporary mock data from production workflows.\n\nIf a feature is not connected yet, display a clear development status rather than fake success.\n\n==================================================\n10. SECURITY\n============\n\nImplement:\n\n* Password hashing.\n* Token-based authentication.\n* Protected backend routes.\n* Input validation.\n* File type validation.\n* File size limits.\n* Safe file handling.\n* User-specific data access.\n* Environment variable configuration.\n\nA user must never be able to access another user\'s resumes or analysis results.\n\nDo not store plaintext passwords.\n\nDo not expose API keys or sensitive configuration in frontend code.\n\n==================================================\n11. ERROR HANDLING\n==================\n\nProvide proper error messages for:\n\n* Invalid login.\n* Invalid file.\n* Failed PDF extraction.\n* Failed DOCX extraction.\n* Empty job description.\n* Invalid job URL.\n* Gemini API failure.\n* Database errors.\n* Failed PDF/DOCX export.\n* Network errors.\n\nDo not silently fail.\n\n==================================================\n12. TESTING\n===========\n\nTest the complete application.\n\nTest these user journeys:\n\nJOURNEY 1:\nSignup \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Dashboard.\n\nJOURNEY 2:\nDashboard \342\206\222 Create Resume \342\206\222 Generate with Gemini \342\206\222 Save Resume \342\206\222 Open Editor.\n\nJOURNEY 3:\nUpload Resume \342\206\222 Add Job Description \342\206\222 Analyse \342\206\222 Receive Score \342\206\222 View EvidenceMap.\n\nJOURNEY 4:\nAnalyse Resume \342\206\222 Improve with AI \342\206\222 TruthGuard Validation \342\206\222 Approve Changes \342\206\222 Save New Version.\n\nJOURNEY 5:\nOpen Editor \342\206\222 Edit Resume \342\206\222 Reanalyse \342\206\222 Download PDF/DOCX.\n\nJOURNEY 6:\nOpen LinkedIn Optimizer \342\206\222 Import Resume \342\206\222 Optimise Profile \342\206\222 Save Changes.\n\nVerify that all user data is saved correctly.\n\n==================================================\n13. FINAL DEVELOPMENT RULES\n===========================\n\n1. Inspect the complete existing application.\n2. Identify incomplete and duplicated implementations.\n3. Reuse existing code.\n4. Implement the backend.\n5. Connect Gemini.\n6. Connect SQLite.\n7. Connect the Resume Score Engine.\n8. Integrate EvidenceMap and TruthGuard.\n9. Connect every frontend workflow.\n10. Test all six user journeys.\n11. Fix all critical errors.\n12. Preserve the existing UI.\n\nDo not replace working components unnecessarily.\n\nDo not generate fake analysis results.\n\nDo not claim a feature is working unless it has actually been tested.\n\nDo not stop after creating files or a development plan.\n\nImplement the integration and run the application.\n\nAt the end, provide:\n\n* Backend setup instructions.\n* Frontend setup instructions.\n* Required environment variables.\n* Gemini API configuration steps.\n* Database setup instructions.\n* List of completed features.\n* List of remaining issues."
    }
  }
}
