  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 3
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Project**: Resume Architect (\"Don\'t just match the job. Prove your fit.\")\n- **Core Request**:\n  - Unify and integrate every feature into one cohesive, full-stack application.\n  - Implement the requested central backend architecture using Python, FastAPI, SQLite (SQLAlchemy ORM), PyMuPDF/python-docx/pdf generation, and Google Gemini API.\n  - Maintain the existing React + Vite + Tailwind CSS frontend without redesigning UI or deleting existing features.\n  - Integrate a central Gemini AI service (`services/gemini_service.py`), deterministic Resume Score Engine (`services/score_engine.py`, 6 weighted categories: Skills 30%, Keywords 20%, Projects 20%, Experience 15%, Education 5%, Formatting 10%), EvidenceMap (`services/evidence_map.py`), and TruthGuard (`services/truthguard.py`).\n  - Implement full REST endpoints: Auth (`/api/auth/*`), Resumes (`/api/resumes/*`), Versions (`/api/resumes/{id}/versions`), Analysis (`/api/analysis/*`), AI Improvement (`/api/resumes/{id}/improve`), Editor (`/api/resumes/{id}/content`), Export (`/api/resumes/{id}/export/pdf`, `/api/resumes/{id}/export/docx`), LinkedIn (`/api/linkedin/*`).\n  - Wire all 6 user journeys end-to-end:\n    1. Signup -> Login -> Dashboard\n    2. Dashboard -> Create Resume -> Generate with Gemini -> Save Resume -> Open Editor\n    3. Upload Resume -> Add JD -> Analyse -> Score -> EvidenceMap\n    4. Analyse -> Improve with AI -> TruthGuard Validation -> Approve -> Save Version\n    5. Editor -> Edit -> Reanalyse -> Download PDF/DOCX\n    6. LinkedIn Optimizer -> Import Resume -> Optimise Profile -> Save Changes\n- **Target URLs / Applet ID**:\n  - Applet ID: `1f4a59a4-792a-4989-a11d-603d71162699`\n  - Dev URL: `https://ais-dev-znkzxpsjihrpkqr2nctcje-956790725848.asia-southeast1.run.app`\n  - User Email: `pavankotha31@gmail.com`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed**:\n  - `src/components/dashboard/LinkedInView.tsx`: Full LinkedIn Profile Optimizer view with 2-panel layout, manual & import modes, and export modal.\n  - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInFormPanel.tsx`: Manual input (tabs for info, headline, about, experience, education, projects, skills, certifications) and resume import modal.\n  - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInAnalysisPanel.tsx`: 7-dimension scoring breakdown, 3 headline generators, 4 About section styles, STAR/XYZ bullet optimizer with TruthGuard badges, EvidenceMap keywords, and live interactive LinkedIn card preview.\n  - `src/components/linkedin/LinkedInExportModal.tsx`: Draft revision manager and section-by-section clipboard copy with mandatory disclaimer notice.\n  - `src/services/linkedInOptimizerService.ts`: LinkedIn client service connecting to `/api/linkedin/optimize` with deterministic local fallback.\n  - `src/utils/linkedInSampleData.ts`: Realistic sample profiles for experienced engineer and student/fresher presets.\n  - `server.ts`: Express mock/proxy server with `/api/linkedin/optimize` and `/api/gemini/generate` handling, passing `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) and Vite compilation.\n- **Skills/Docs Inspected**:\n  - `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md`: Read in full. Key takeaway: Use `@google/genai` or Google GenAI Python SDK (`google-genai`), model `gemini-3.8-flash` (or environment configured model via `GEMINI_MODEL`), never expose API keys on client, API key from `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n- **In Progress / To Be Started**:\n  - Central backend in `backend/` directory with FastAPI, SQLite, SQLAlchemy, PyMuPDF, python-docx, and central Gemini service.\n  - Bridging frontend Vite proxy / Express server to route `/api/*` requests to the FastAPI backend (or running FastAPI alongside or unified via reverse proxy).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Runtime Environment**:\n  - AI Studio preview container runs on port 3000.\n  - The current setup uses `tsx server.ts` running Express that mounts Vite middlewares (`vite.middlewares`).\n  - Python 3 is available in the Linux container (`bash` shell available via `run_command`).\n  - To support the Python FastAPI backend cleanly within the AI Studio architecture (where the outer dev server expects port 3000):\n    - FastAPI can run on an internal port (e.g., port 8000 via Uvicorn).\n    - `server.ts` (Express) can proxy all `/api/*` calls directly to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/*` using `http-proxy-middleware`, or FastAPI can run as a managed child process/daemon started alongside the server.\n    - Alternatively, check if Python dependencies (`fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `sqlalchemy`, `pydantic`, `pymupdf`, `python-docx`, `google-genai`, `passlib[bcrypt]`, `python-jose` or `pyjwt`) can be installed via `pip install` in the container.\n- **Score Engine Weights (Mandatory)**:\n  - Technical Skills Alignment: 30%\n  - Keyword Alignment: 20%\n  - Project Relevance: 20%\n  - Experience Relevance: 15%\n  - Education Relevance: 5%\n  - Formatting and Readability: 10%\n  - Formula: `Final Score = (Skills * 0.30) + (Keywords * 0.20) + (Projects * 0.20) + (Experience * 0.15) + (Education * 0.05) + (Formatting * 0.10)`. All scores 0\342\200\223100, deterministic, no double-counting.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1**: `server.ts(999,17): error TS2322: Type \'\"concise\" | \"fresher\" | \"professional\" | \"technical\"\' is not assignable to type \'never\'`\n  - *Cause*: Indexing `dynamicAbout[s]` where `s` was typed as a union of string literals failed strict property type checking.\n  - *Fix*: Cast `(dynamicAbout as any)[s]` and defined `const styles = [\'professional\', \'fresher\', \'technical\', \'concise\'] as const`.\n- **Error 2**: `server.ts(1036,39): error TS7006: Parameter \'e\' implicitly has an \'any\' type`\n  - *Cause*: `experienceOptimizations.some((e) => ...)` lacked explicit typing in TS strict mode.\n  - *Fix*: Changed to `(e: any) => e.truthGuardStatus === \'NEEDS CONFIRMATION\'`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Frontend compiles cleanly (`compile_applet` passed, `lint_applet` passed).\n- Dev server is currently running.\n- Backend directory `backend/` has not yet been populated.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Verify Python & Dependencies**:\n   - Check `python3 --version` and `pip` in the workspace using `run_command`.\n   - Create `backend/requirements.txt` containing:\n     `fastapi`, `uvicorn[standard]`, `sqlalchemy`, `pydantic`, `pymupdf` (fitz), `python-docx`, `google-genai`, `passlib[bcrypt]`, `pyjwt`, `python-multipart`, `aiofiles`, `reportlab`.\n   - Install dependencies in Python environment.\n2. **Build Backend Architecture (`backend/app/`)**:\n   - `core/config.py`: Settings using `pydantic-settings` or `os.environ` (`DATABASE_URL = \"sqlite:///./resume_architect.db\"`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_MODEL = \"gemini-3.8-flash\"`, `JWT_SECRET`).\n   - `core/security.py`: Password hashing (bcrypt), JWT create/verify tokens.\n   - `database/connection.py`: SQLAlchemy engine, session maker, base declarative.\n   - `database/models.py`: User, CandidateProfile, Resume, ResumeVersion, ResumeAnalysis, LinkedInProfile, Activity.\n   - `schemas/`: `resume_schema.py`, `analysis_schema.py`, `linkedin_schema.py`, `auth_schema.py`.\n   - `services/`:\n     - `gemini_service.py`: Central service using `google-genai` with structured JSON, fallback error handling, supporting operations A-E (`CREATE_RESUME`, `REVIEW_RESUME`, `IMPROVE_RESUME`, `OPTIMIZE_LINKEDIN`, `TRUTHGUARD_VALIDATE`).\n     - `score_engine.py`: Independent deterministic 6-category score engine with exact weights (30/20/20/15/5/10).\n     - `evidence_map.py`: Computes MATCHED, PARTIALLY MATCHED, NOT FOUND.\n     - `truthguard.py`: Validates claims with SUPPORTED, NEEDS_CONFIRMATION, UNSUPPORTED.\n     - `resume_parser.py`: PyMuPDF and python-docx text & structure extractor.\n     - `export_service.py`: PDF & DOCX generation for resumes.\n     - `resume_service.py` & `linkedin_service.py`.\n   - `api/`: `auth.py`, `resumes.py`, `analysis.py`, `editor.py`, `linkedin.py`.\n   - `main.py`: FastAPI application mounting all routers under `/api`.\n3. **Bridge Express Dev Server to FastAPI Backend**:\n   - In `server.ts`, spawn/daemonize uvicorn on `http://127.0.0.1:8000` (or run as background task).\n   - Use `http-proxy-middleware` in `server.ts` to proxy all `/api/*` traffic to the FastAPI backend running on port 8000, ensuring seamless integration on port 3000.\n4. **Wire Frontend Services to Backend Endpoints**:\n   - Verify `src/services/authService.ts`, `src/services/resumeService.ts`, `src/services/analysisService.ts`, `src/services/linkedInOptimizerService.ts` make genuine HTTP calls to `/api/*`.\n5. **Verify All 6 User Journeys**:\n   - Test Signup/Login, Resume Creation, Reviewer & EvidenceMap upload, AI Improvement with TruthGuard, Editor export, and LinkedIn Optimizer end-to-end.\n6. **Documentation**:\n   - Provide backend/frontend setup instructions, environment variables (`.env.example`), Gemini config steps, database migration notes, completed features, and remaining issues.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Preserve Existing UI**: Forest-green (`#1B4332`), cream background (`#FAF8F5`), crisp borders (`#E5E1D7`), zero UI redesign or component regressions.\n- **TruthGuard & Anti-Hallucination**: Never auto-insert unverified facts or fabricated metrics.\n- **Deterministic Scoring**: Numerical match score (0\342\200\223100) must be computed by the Python score engine with documented weights, not arbitrary LLM hallucinated numbers.\n- **No API Keys in Frontend**: Keep all Gemini calls exclusively on the backend.\n</summary>"
