      text: "You are a senior full-stack developer and UI/UX designer. Build the foundation of a professional web application called **Resume Architect**.\n\nPROJECT NAME: Resume Architect\n\nTAGLINE: Don\'t just match the job. Prove your fit.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nUse the finalised Resume Architect UI reference image as the visual design blueprint if it is available. Maintain the same visual identity throughout the entire application.\n\nFor this task, build ONLY:\n\n1. Project setup and folder structure.\n2. Global design system.\n3. Landing page.\n4. Login page.\n5. Signup page.\n\nDo not build the other application pages yet.\n\n---\n\n1. TECHNOLOGY STACK\n\n---\n\nFrontend:\n\n* React.js\n* Vite\n* JavaScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* React Router\n* Lucide React icons\n\nUse clean, reusable React components.\n\nPrepare the project so that a Python FastAPI backend and Gemini AI API can be integrated later.\n\n---\n\n2. DESIGN SYSTEM\n\n---\n\nThe website must look like a real professional SaaS product, not a generic AI-generated website.\n\nVisual style:\n\n* Warm off-white / cream background.\n* Forest green as the primary accent.\n* Charcoal text.\n* Subtle light grey borders.\n* Clean typography.\n* Generous spacing.\n* Rounded cards with subtle shadows.\n* Minimal animations and smooth transitions.\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Excessive gradients.\n* Neon colours.\n* Excessive glassmorphism.\n* Unnecessary animations.\n* Overcrowded layouts.\n* Generic futuristic AI designs.\n\nThe interface must be responsive on desktop, tablet and mobile.\n\n---\n\n3. LANDING PAGE\n\n---"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Build the foundation of a professional web application called RESUME ARCHITECT.\n\nTAGLINE: Don\'t just match the job. Prove your fit.\n\nIMPORTANT PRODUCT DIRECTION:\n\nResume Architect is primarily an AI-powered resume analysis, scoring and improvement platform.\n\nThe most important feature is the AI Resume Score Engine.\n\nDo not introduce unnecessary features such as:\n\n* Pricing pages\n* Subscription plans\n* Payment gateways\n* Premium memberships\n* Price engines\n* Billing systems\n\nAll core resume-building, reviewing, editing and LinkedIn optimization features should be accessible without payment-related restrictions.\n\nTECHNOLOGY:\n\n* React.js\n* Vite\n* JavaScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* React Router\n* Lucide React\n\nDESIGN:\nFollow the finalised Resume Architect UI reference.\n\nUse:\n\n* Warm off-white background.\n* Forest green accents.\n* Charcoal typography.\n* Clean professional cards.\n* Subtle borders and shadows.\n* Minimal animations.\n* Responsive layouts.\n\nAvoid excessive gradients, neon colours and futuristic AI styling.\n\nBUILD ONLY THESE COMPONENTS:\n\n1. LANDING PAGE\n\nInclude:\n\n* Resume Architect logo.\n* Navigation bar.\n* Hero section.\n* Features section.\n* How It Works section.\n* Footer.\n\nHero heading:\n\n\"Build, Improve and Showcase a Resume That Gets You Hired.\"\n\nDescription:\n\n\"Analyse your resume, measure your job compatibility, discover skill gaps and create a professional resume with AI assistance.\"\n\nHighlight these four features:\n\nA. AI Resume Score Engine\nAnalyse resumes against job descriptions and calculate a transparent match score.\n\nB. Resume Builder\nCreate ATS-conscious resumes using candidate information.\n\nC. Resume Reviewer\nIdentify skill gaps, missing keywords and formatting issues.\n\nD. LinkedIn Optimizer\nImprove LinkedIn headlines, About sections, experience and skills.\n\n2. LOGIN PAGE\n\nFields:\n\n* Email.\n* Password.\n* Show/hide password.\n* Remember me.\n* Forgot password.\n* Login button.\n* Signup navigation.\n\n3. SIGNUP PAGE\n\nFields:\n\n* Full name.\n* Email.\n* Password.\n* Confirm password.\n* Create account button.\n\nInclude basic frontend validation.\n\n4. AUTHENTICATION FOUNDATION\n\nImplement temporary local development authentication.\n\nKeep authentication logic separate so it can later connect to FastAPI and a database.\n\nDo not present localStorage authentication as production-secure.\n\n5. SCORE ENGINE FOUNDATION\n\nPrepare the project architecture for a central Resume Score Engine.\n\nThe future score engine must evaluate:\n\n* Job description keyword alignment.\n* Technical skill alignment.\n* Project relevance.\n* Work experience relevance.\n* Education relevance.\n* Resume formatting and readability.\n\nPrepare reusable components for:\n\n* Score display.\n* Circular percentage indicator.\n* Category-wise score breakdown.\n* Missing keyword list.\n* Skill gap analysis.\n* Improvement recommendations.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not create a fake score or randomly generate percentages.\n\nThe actual scoring engine will be implemented in a later development phase using backend logic.\n\nThe AI model must not independently invent the final score. The backend scoring engine will calculate it using a transparent, consistent scoring method.\n\n6. PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\nCreate a clean, reusable React project structure.\n\nSeparate:\n\n* Components.\n* Pages.\n* Services.\n* Styles.\n* Layouts.\n* Utilities.\n\nKeep the architecture ready for future integration with:\n\n* Python FastAPI.\n* Gemini AI API.\n* SQLite database.\n* PDF and DOCX processing.\n\n7. DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS\n\n* Inspect the existing project before making changes.\n* Preserve useful existing code.\n* Build the actual working pages.\n* Ensure navigation works.\n* Validate forms.\n* Ensure responsive design.\n* Fix console and build errors.\n* Run the application and test it.\n\nDo not build the Resume Studio, Resume Reviewer, Resume Editor or LinkedIn Optimizer pages yet.\n\nFor this phase, complete the project foundation, design system, landing page, login and signup.\n\nWhen finished, explain the files created, features implemented and how to run the application.\n\nDo not stop at planning. Implement the working application."
    }
