  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Backend Service**\n\nOkay, so I\'m really getting into it now. My focus has shifted to the `backend/app/services/truthguard.py` file. I\'m building out the key components for claim validation, specifically focusing on unsupported metrics, unverifiable stats, and hallucinated claims. Task-483 is on track to finish configuring the broader setup.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1206585"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import re\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\\n\\ndef audit_truthguard(resume_text: str, original_notes: str = \\\"\\\") -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    TruthGuard Anti-Hallucination & Claim Verification Service.\\n    Inspects bullet points and claims to ensure no fabricated statistics or ungrounded claims.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    lines = [l.strip() for l in resume_text.split(\'\\\\n\') if l.strip()]\\n    flags = []\\n\\n    for line in lines:\\n        if len(line) < 20:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Check for high percentage claims\\n        pct_match = re.search(r\'(\\\\b\\\\d{2,3}%\\\\b)\', line)\\n        if pct_match:\\n            pct = pct_match.group(1)\\n            flags.append({\\n                \\\"claim\\\": line[:100] + (\\\"...\\\" if len(line) > 100 else \\\"\\\"),\\n                \\\"status\\\": \\\"NEEDS_CONFIRMATION\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": f\\\"Detected specific metric \'{pct}\'. Ensure this measurement is backed by verifiable production analytics.\\\",\\n                \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Confirm whether this was measured via internal APM/benchmarks before client submission.\\\"\\n            })\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Check for vague buzzwords without technical grounding\\n        if re.search(r\'\\\\b(spearheaded|revolutionized|groundbreaking|world-class|best-in-class)\\\\b\', line, re.I):\\n            flags.append({\\n                \\\"claim\\\": line[:100] + (\\\"...\\\" if len(line) > 100 else \\\"\\\"),\\n                \\\"status\\\": \\\"NEEDS_CONFIRMATION\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Subjective hyperbole detected. Recruiters and hiring managers prefer concrete technical outcomes over adjectives.\\\",\\n                \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Replace adjectives with quantifiable actions (e.g., \'Architected system with 99.9% uptime\').\\\"\\n            })\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Check for strong technical action verbs with clear scope\\n        if re.search(r\'^(developed|engineered|implemented|designed|built|reduced|scaled|deployed|refactored)\\\\b\', line, re.I):\\n            flags.append({\\n                \\\"claim\\\": line[:100] + (\\\"...\\\" if len(line) > 100 else \\\"\\\"),\\n                \\\"status\\\": \\\"SUPPORTED\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Direct active verb demonstrating individual engineering responsibility.\\\",\\n                \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Approved for inclusion in final ATS resume.\\\"\\n            })\\n\\n    # Return top 5-7 meaningful flags\\n    return flags[:7]\\n\", \"Description\":\"TruthGuard verification service\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/backend/app/services/truthguard.py\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing truthguard.py\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create truthguard.py\"}"
