  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Infrastructure Setup**\n\nI\'m noticing the clean structure of this setup. In `server.ts`, I\'m planning to spawn the Python FastAPI Uvicorn process on `127.0.0.1:8000` during `startServer()`. I\'m going to leverage `spawn` from `child_process`, and I\'m looking at using `createProxyMiddleware` for routing.\n\n\n**Implementing Proxy Strategy**\n\nI\'ve got the proxy strategy down now. All `/api/*` routes are going to FastAPI on `127.0.0.1:8000` thanks to `createProxyMiddleware`. This placement makes sure requests hit the Python backend. The `changeOrigin: true` setting is also crucial. Now, any request on `/api` hits the Python backend.\n\n\n**Defining API Routes**\n\nI\'m now mapping out specific API endpoints: `/api/auth/signup`, `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/me`, the resume-related routes, analysis endpoints, LinkedIn optimization, health checks, and Gemini-based generation routes. I\'m also considering fallback mechanisms with `createProxyMiddleware`, and how Express might handle errors and potential Python backend downtime. I need to figure out what happens if python is down.\n\n\n"
